sv.DictReader(f))\n\nnames = set()\nfor r in rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv'):\n    names.add(r['home_team']); names.add(r['away_team'])\nfor r in rows('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv'):\n    names.add(r['home_team']); names.add(r['away_team'])\nnovo = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nfor r in novo:\n    names.add(r['Equipe_mandante']); names.add(r['Equipe_visitante'])\nbrf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nfor r in brf:\n    names.add(r['home']); names.add(r['away'])\nprint(len(names), \"unique names in match data\")\nfor n in sorted(names):\n    print(repr(n))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788230527311,"end":1788230527317}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting notes:\n- Brasileirao_Matches seasons 2012-2022 (4,180)\n- Cup rounds 1-8 (final = max round per season... actually Copa do Brasil rounds per season vary: 2012 had 8 rounds? Actually Copa do Brasil 2012 had 8 rounds? The 2012 edition had rounds up to 8? Wait, cup format: 2012 had 5 knockout rounds... hmm, round values 1-8 across seasons. The \"final\" = max round for that season, and the final is a 2-legged tie (home and away). I'll define final = matches in max round of each season.)\n- Libertadores goals are strings; fine. Stages include \"final\" — great, \"Find all Copa Libertadores finals\" works via stage=final.\n- BR-Football tournaments: Serie A, Serie B, Serie C, Copa do Brasil — team names without accents? \"Sao Paulo\" no accent. So normalization needs accent-insensitive matching to link \"Sao Paulo\" ↔ \"São Paulo\".\n- Novo: 2003-2019, Vencedor values Mandante/Empate/Visitante. Teams like \"América-MG\", \"Athletico-PR\", \"Barueri\".\n- FIFA clubs — my filter was wrong (I filtered nationality=Brazil for clubs list — oops, that lists clubs of Brazilian players). Fine.\n\nTeam name variants across files (examples):\n- \"Palmeiras-SP\" (Brasileirao), \"Palmeiras\" (BR-Football? let me check), \"S.E. Palmeiras\"?\n- \"América-MG\" (novo), \"America-MG\" (Brasileirao), \"América - MG\" (cup)\n- \"Athletico-PR\" vs \"Atlético-PR\" vs \"Atletico Paranaense\"\n- \"Sao Paulo\" vs \"São Paulo\"\n\nStrategy for canonical keys: strip accents, lowercase, remove spaces/punctuation, strip state suffix patterns like `-mg`, `-sp`, ` - mg`, `-(mg)`, and trailing country codes ` (uru)`. Then map via alias table for known distinct clubs that could collide? Risk: \"Atlético-MG\" vs \"Atlético-GO\" differ by suffix, which we must keep as part of identity (they're different clubs!). So stripping state suffix for identity is WRONG for those cases unless the state is part of the club's canonical identity. Hmm.\n\nKey insight: State suffixes distinguish \"Atlético-MG\" from \"Atlético-GO\" and \"América-MG\" from \"América-RN\" and \"Atlético-PR\" from \"Atlético-MG\". These clubs are conventionally named WITH the state qualifier. But \"Palmeiras-SP\" should be just \"Palmeiras\".\n\nThe state suffix is part of the canonical name only when the club is commonly known by city/state disambiguation: América-MG, América-RN, Atlético-MG, Atlético-GO, Atlético-PR (Athletico), Avaí-SC (known as Avaí), Botafogo-RJ (known as Botafogo), Ceará-CE (known as Ceará), Goiás-GO (known as Goiás), etc.\n\nMost suffixes are redundant; some are essential (Atlético-MG/GO/PR, América-MG/RN).\n\nApproach: maintain a curated ALIAS map from normalized variant → canonical display name. I'll enumerate clubs from the datasets (they're a bounded set — Brazilian clubs ~60-80 unique) and build the alias table programmatically by inspecting unique names. Let me dump all unique team names across the 5 match files and design the alias table.\n\nAlso FIFA clubs: \"Flamengo\" appears as \"Flamengo\"? Check FIFA club names for Brazilian clubs: likely \"Flamengo\", \"Palmeiras\", \"São Paulo\", \"Santos\", \"Grêmio\", \"Internacional\", \"Corinthians\", \"Cruzeiro\", \"Atlético Mineiro\"?, \"Athletico Paranaense\"?, \"Bahia\", \"Sport\", \"Vasco\", \"Fortaleza\", etc. Cross-file linking FIFA club → match team needs its own alias layer. Let me dump Brazilian-club names in FIFA too.\n\nLet me collect unique names.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ad86906001QCt7luo9EOqV3H","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05ad7d64c001OgvtNV1085d5tN"}}
