 Remo\" wouldn't match \"Remo\" via suffix strip; add alias).\n\n  Actually, since this is a curated alias layer anyway, I'll do BOTH: (a) strip trailing FC/EC/SC/AC tokens in key-building, (b) curated alias map for remaining oddballs. With (a): \"Fortaleza FC\"→fortaleza ✓, \"EC Bahia\"? leading \"EC \" not trailing — alias. \"Vitoria EC\"→vitoria ✓ but which vitoria? bare vitoria default BA ✓. \"America FC Natal\": strip \"FC\"? it's mid-name: \"america fc natal\" — trailing token is \"natal\". Alias needed anyway.\n\n  Careful with (a) stripping \"SC\": \"EC Internacional SC\" → internacionalsc... trailing SC stripped → \"internacional\" → default RS — it IS Internacional-SC (Lages)! Merging with Internacional-RS would be wrong. Hmm. \"EC Internacional SC\" — Internacional Santa Maria? Actually \"Inter de Santa Maria (RS)\"... The cup data may include \"EC Internacional SC\" = Internacional de Lages? Ugh. Low-stakes demo; the alias map wins for known clubs; generic suffix strip is best-effort. I'll include \"internacional sc\" → internacional+SC alias to be safe. Actually let me NOT overthink tiny Serie C clubs — the spec's core requirement: \"Handles team name variations correctly\" for the main clubs. I'll ensure all top-tier clubs + common variants are right, and generic parsing handles the rest consistently.\n\nFIFA club linking (cross-file): FIFA clubs for Brazilian players: \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\", \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Atlético Paranaense\", \"Bahia\", \"Botafogo\", \"Ceará Sporting Club\", \"Chapecoense\", \"Cruzeiro\", \"Fluminense\", \"Grêmio\", \"Internacional\", \"Paraná\", \"Santos\", \"Sport Club do Recife\", \"Vitória\", plus \"Flamengo\"?? Wait — Flamengo isn't in the list! Brazilian players' clubs list lacks Flamengo, Palmeiras, São Paulo, Vasco, Corinthians... The FIFA dataset (FIFA 19, 2018) includes clubs of ALL players; I filtered by Nationality=Brazil which shows clubs having ≥1 Brazilian player. Flamengo/Palmeiras/Corinthians/São Paulo aren't there?! That means the dataset's Brazilian clubs list is sparse — big Brazilian clubs may be labeled differently or absent. Let me check: search Club field containing \"Flamengo\"/\"Palmeiras\"/\"Sao Paulo\"/\"São Paulo\"/\"Corinthians\"/\"Vasco\" across all rows. FIFA 19 did include Brazilian league teams... The dataset might have different club naming. Let me check.\n\nAlso player search \"Gabriel Barbosa\" — FIFA 19 has \"Gabriel Barbosa\" (Gabigol) at Santos/Inter Milan. Good.\n\nLet me verify FIFA club coverage quickly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05adc6c18001F2LRHLektrcEuR","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05ad98a63001dz9fWHka9BCtaG"}}
