{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788230911419,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_477cb4650fdf4c8aa0707f5d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\ndef rows(p):\n    with open(p, newline='', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbrf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nyears = defaultdict(lambda: [None, None])\nfor r in brf:\n    y = r['date'][:4]\n    lo, hi = years[r['tournament']]\n    years[r['tournament']] = [min(lo, y) if lo else y, max(hi, y) if hi else y]\nprint(\"BR-Football year ranges:\", dict(years))\nbad_goals = sum(1 for r in brf if not r['home_goal'].strip() or not r['away_goal'].strip())\nprint(\"empty goals:\", bad_goals, \"of\", len(brf))\n# duplicate (tournament, date, home, away)?\nk = Counter((r['tournament'], r['date'], r['home'], r['away']) for r in brf)\nprint(\"dup keys in BR-Football:\", sum(1 for c in k.values() if c > 1))\n\nnovo = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nprint(\"novo dup (Ano, mand, visit):\", sum(1 for c in Counter((r['Ano'], r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante']) for r in novo).values() if c > 1))\nprint(\"novo obs values:\", Counter(r.get('OBS','') for r in novo).most_common(3))\n\ncup = rows('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\nprint(\"cup dup (season,date,home,away):\", sum(1 for c in Counter((r['season'], r['datetime'][:10], r['home_team'], r['away_team']) for r in cup).values() if c > 1))\n\nbr = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nprint(\"br dup (season,round,home,away):\", sum(1 for c in Counter((r['season'], r['round'], r['home_team'], r['away_team']) for r in br).values() if c > 1))\nprint(\"br empty goals:\", sum(1 for r in br if not r['home_goal'].strip() or not r['away_goal'].strip()))\nEOF"},"output":"BR-Football year ranges: {'Copa do Brasil': ['2014', '2023'], 'Serie A': ['2014', '2023'], 'Serie B': ['2014', '2023'], 'Serie C': ['2014', '2023']}\nempty goals: 0 of 10296\ndup keys in BR-Football: 0\nnovo dup (Ano, mand, visit): 1\nnovo obs values: [('', 6875), ('REMARCADO', 11)]\ncup dup (season,date,home,away): 0\nbr dup (season,round,home,away): 0\nbr empty goals: 0\n","metadata":{"output":"BR-Football year ranges: {'Copa do Brasil': ['2014', '2023'], 'Serie A': ['2014', '2023'], 'Serie B': ['2014', '2023'], 'Serie C': ['2014', '2023']}\nempty goals: 0 of 10296\ndup keys in BR-Football: 0\nnovo dup (Ano, mand, visit): 1\nnovo obs values: [('', 6875), ('REMARCADO', 11)]\ncup dup (season,date,home,away): 0\nbr dup (season,round,home,away): 0\nbr empty goals: 0\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\ndef rows(p):\n    with open(p, newline='', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbrf = rows('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv')\nyears = defaultdict(lambda: [None, None])\nfor r in brf:\n    y = r['date'][:4]\n    lo, hi = years[r['tournament']]\n    years[r['tournament']] = [min(lo, y) if lo else y, max(hi, y) if hi else y]\nprint(\"BR-Football year ranges:\", dict(years))\nbad_goals = sum(1 for r in brf if not r['home_goal'].strip() or not r['away_goal'].strip())\nprint(\"empty goals:\", bad_goals, \"of\", len(brf))\n# duplicate (tournament, date, home, away)?\nk = Counter((r['tournament'], r['date'], r['home'], r['away']) for r in brf)\nprint(\"dup keys in BR-Football:\", sum(1 for c in k.values() if c > 1))\n\nnovo = rows('data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv')\nprint(\"novo dup (Ano, mand, visit):\", sum(1 for c in Counter((r['Ano'], r['Equipe_mandante'], r['Equipe_visitante']) for r in novo).values() if c > 1))\nprint(\"novo obs values:\", Counter(r.get('OBS','') for r in novo).most_common(3))\n\ncup = rows('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv')\nprint(\"cup dup (season,date,home,away):\", sum(1 for c in Counter((r['season'], r['datetime'][:10], r['home_team'], r['away_team']) for r in cup).values() if c > 1))\n\nbr = rows('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv')\nprint(\"br dup (season,round,home,away):\", sum(1 for c in Counter((r['season'], r['round'], r['home_team'], r['away_team']) for r in br).values() if c > 1))\nprint(\"br empty goals:\", sum(1 for r in br if not r['home_goal'].strip() or not r['away_goal'].strip()))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788230911411,"end":1788230911417}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The FIFA dataset is FIFA 19 (2018) and does NOT include the Brazilian Série A clubs (they were removed from FIFA 19's dataset in this Kaggle export, apparently). Brazilian clubs present: \"Atlético Mineiro\", \"Atlético Paranaense\", \"Bahia\", \"Botafogo\", \"Ceará Sporting Club\", \"Chapecoense\", \"Cruzeiro\", \"Fluminense\", \"Grêmio\", \"Internacional\", \"Paraná\", \"Santos\", \"Sport Club do Recife\", \"Vitória\", \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\". So cross-file queries (player + match data) will link on those. Gabriel Barbosa isn't in the dataset (he was at Inter/Benfica in FIFA19? — search says no). Fine — \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" returns empty gracefully; tests should use Neymar Jr, Alisson, Casemiro per spec examples.\n\nThe spec example says \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" — Flamengo won't match in FIFA data (returns empty). That's a data reality; my tools handle gracefully. The spec's example answer shows Neymar/Alisson/Casemiro — those work.\n\nNow, architecture plan (final):\n\n**Files:**\n1. `brazilian_soccer/__init__.py` — package docstring + version.\n2. `brazilian_soccer/normalize.py` — accents, keys, date parsing, number parsing, team name parsing (state/country codes), alias table.\n3. `brazilian_soccer/models.py` — dataclasses: Match, Player, TeamRegistry/Club.\n4. `brazilian_soccer/data_loader.py` — load the 6 CSVs → normalized Matches/Players.\n5. `brazilian_soccer/store.py` — SoccerStore: indexes, competitions catalog, queries (search_matches, players...).\n6. `brazilian_soccer/analytics.py` — standings, h2h, team stats, aggregates, derbies, biggest wins.\n7. `brazilian_soccer/tools.py` — the MCP tool functions (thin wrappers returning JSON-safe dicts) + registry list.\n8. `server.py` — FastMCP app wiring tools + resources; `main()` stdio.\n9. `tests/…` — BDD feature files + steps + unit tests + MCP e2e test.\n10. `requirements.txt`, `README.md` update, maybe `pyproject.toml` not needed.\n\nEach code file gets a context block comment at the top (prompts.txt hints at \"detailed context block comment at the start of every code file\" — that was from the sample prompt, not our TASK.md; TASK.md doesn't require it. I'll include brief module docstrings — good practice, not excessive).\n\n**Competition naming:** normalize to canonical labels:\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv → \"Brasileirão Serie A\" (source: kaggle jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro)\n- Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv → \"Copa do Brasil\"\n- Libertadores_Matches.csv → \"Copa Libertadores\"\n- BR-Football-Dataset.csv → keep `tournament` value: \"Serie A\", \"Serie B\", \"Serie C\", \"Copa do Brasil\" → normalize to \"Brasileirão Serie A/B/C\", \"Copa do Brasil\" — but mark dataset source. To keep queries clean I'll set competition = normalized tournament name: \"Serie A\" → \"Brasileirão Serie A\"? Hmm that conflates with dataset 1 but they're both Série A — that's semantically correct and enables richer queries (2023 Série A lives only in BR-Football). I'll add a `source`/dataset field on matches so provenance is queryable.\n- novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv → \"Brasileirão Serie A\" with source note? It covers 2003–2019. It's Campeonato Brasileiro Série A (2003-2019 per Kaggle title). Mark source.\n\nFor `search_matches(competition=...)` I'll accept fuzzy competition matching (case-insensitive accent-strip substring/alias): \"brasileirao\" → matches both \"Brasileirão Serie A\" entries; \"serie a\", \"libertadores\", \"copa do brasil\", \"serie b\"...\n\n**Season:** all datasets have season/Ano. BR-Football has date only → season = date.year (fine for Série A/B; Copa do Brasil spans years sometimes but ok).\n\n**Rounds:** Brasileirao round int; cup round int (finals = max round per season... wait cup round up to 8; 2012 Copa do Brasil had rounds 1..8? Actually 2012 had 5 rounds? The data shows rounds 1-8. Per-season max differs. I'll expose `stage` for cup as: if round == max(round in season) → \"final\"; also semis = max-1? Keep simple: provide `round` and a derived `stage` = \"final\" when round == season max, else f\"round {round}\". Libertadores: stage given (\"group stage\", \"round of 16\", \"quarterfinals\", \"semifinals\", \"final\").\n- `search_matches(stage=\"final\")` matches Libertadores stage and derived cup finals and Brasileirão? Brasileirão has no final. Good.\n\n**Derbies:** curated dict of rivalries by canonical key pairs: fla-flu (flamengo|fluminense), clásico dos milhões (flamengo|vasco), botafogo-flamengo? (Clássico Vovô), majestoso (corinthians|são paulo), choque-rei (palmeiras|são paulo), dérbi paulista (corinthians|palmeiras), paulista (palmeiras|corinthians same), grenal (grêmio|internacional), atletiba (athletico-pr|coritiba), paranaense (athletico|parana clube), ba-vi (bahia|vitoria), clássico rei? , penalidade... include: fla-flu, clássico-dos-milhões (flamengo-vasco), clássico-vovô (botafogo-flamengo), botafogo-fluminense (clássico-vovô? no, that's \"Taca Rio\"?) keep the famous ones: Fla-Flu, Fla-Vasco (Clássico dos Milhões), Botafogo × Flamengo (Clássico da Rivalidade), Grenal, Dérbi Paulista (Palmeiras × Corinthians), Majestoso (Corinthians × São Paulo), Choque-Rei (Palmeiras × São Paulo), Atletiba (Athletico-PR × Coritiba), Ba-Vi (Bahia × Vitória), Clássico dos Guaranis? no. Also Pépino? Keep 9-10. Plus \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" → matches where (home,away) is a derby pair, in season 2023.\n\n**Standings:** for