— pick \"Athletico-PR\" (data majority).\n  Actually — simpler uniform rule: display = accented-base + \"-\" + code when ambiguous, else accented base; accented base chosen as the most frequent accented form. For atletico base: forms \"Atlético\", \"Atletico\" — most frequent probably \"Atlético\". So display \"Atlético-MG\", \"Atlético-PR\", \"Atlético-GO\", \"Atlético-AC\"... fine, consistent. FIFA club \"Atlético Mineiro\" → alias → atletico|MG → display \"Atlético-MG\" — cross-file link works on KEY not display. \n- \"vasco da gama\" → (\"vasco\",\"RJ\"); bare \"vasco\" → default RJ.\n- \"athletico\" (bare) → (\"atletico\",\"PR\")\n- \"america fc minas gerais\" (FIFA, after paren-strip) → (\"america\",\"MG\")\n- \"america de cali\" → own club, no change.\n- \"sport club do recife\"/\"sport recife\" → (\"sport\",\"PE\"); \"sport\" bare → default PE.\n- \"ceara sporting club\" → (\"ceara\", None) — ceara unambiguous → key \"ceara\" ✓.\n- \"ec bahia\" → (\"bahia\", None) unambiguous ✓.\n- \"fortaleza fc\"/\"fortaleza ec\" → (\"fortaleza\", None) ✓ (fortaleza states {CE}? bare + CE → single → unify).\n- \"america rn\"? parses \"America RN\" → base america code RN ✓.\n- \"brasil de pelotas\" → (\"brasil\",\"RS\") (base brasil has only RS? \"Brasil - RS\" + \"Brasil de Pelotas\" → codes {RS} → unify → key \"brasil\" display \"Brasil de Pelotas\"? display picks most common raw → \"Brasil - RS\"... ugly. Curated DISPLAY overrides for prettiness — optional. I'll allow display override table for a handful: brasil → \"Brasil de Pelotas\". Meh, skip — not critical. Actually display \"Brasil\" is misleading... add small display map: brasil → \"Brasil de Pelotas\", river → \"Ríver-PI\"? river codes {PI} only (River - PI, River (PI), River AC aliased to PI, Ríver - PI) → key \"river\" display \"Ríver\"... add \"River-PI\". Skip; minor.)\n- \"boavista sc saquarema\" → (\"boavista\",\"RJ\"); boavista codes {RJ} → unify ✓.\n- \"clube do remo\" → (\"remo\",None) ✓ remo unambiguous.\n- \"nautico capibaribe\" → (\"nautico\",None) codes {PE} ✓.\n- \"desportiva ferroviaria\" → (\"desportiva\",\"ES\"); desportiva codes {ES} ✓.\n- \"ser caxias\" → (\"caxias\",None)? caxias codes {RS} ✓ unify.\n- \"cs alagoano\" → (\"csa\",None) ✓.\n- \"operario ferroviario esporte c\" → (\"operario\",\"PR\") — operario codes {PR,MS,MT} ambiguous; without alias the long form becomes its own club — alias fixes.\n- \"guarani de juazeiro\"? distinct from Guarani-SP ✓ (base differs).\n- \"gremio anapolis\" vs \"gremio\" ✓ distinct bases.\n- \"juazeiro\"? fine.\n- \"atletico alagoinhas\" vs \"atletico\" base: \"Atletico Alagoinhas\" — is base \"atletico alagoinhas\" ✓ distinct club (BA). Fine, stays own club.\n- \"atletico acreano\" — own ✓.\n- \"fc atletico cearense\" & \"atletico cearense - ce\": base \"fc atletico cearense\"→ strip leading FC? My suffix-strip only handles TRAILING tokens. \"FC Atlético Cearense\" → key \"fc atletico cearense\" ≠ \"atletico cearense\". Add leading \"fc \" strip too? Careful: \"FC Cascavel\" & \"Fc Cascavel - PR\" ✓ same either way. \"FC Porto\" → key \"porto\"?? Only relevant to FIFA clubs. Leading strip of \"fc \"/\"ec \"/\"sc \"/\"ac \" — \"EC Vitoria\" → \"vitoria\" ✓ good. \"FC Bayern München\" → \"bayern münchen\" harmless. I'll strip leading AND trailing club-type tokens (fc, ec, sc, ac, cf, esporte clube?) from KEYS only. Risk: \"ABC\" → not stripped (not a token). \"CRB\" fine. Hmm \"CSA\" fine. \"ASA\" fine. \"ACE\"? not a token I strip. OK.\n  Wait danger: \"Vitoria F. C. - ES\" → dots stripped in canonical_text → \"vitoria f c es\"?? Order of operations! parse trailing code BEFORE dot-stripping? \"Vitoria F. C. - ES\": trailing token \"ES\" preceded by \"-\". My parser regex should handle \" - ES\" → base \"Vitoria F. C.\" code ES. Then key: strip dots → \"vitoria f c\" → strip trailing \"c\"?? tokens stripped are fc/ec/sc/ac/cf — \"vitoria f c\" tokens: trailing \"c\" — no. Hmm dots→space then \"f c\" doesn't equal \"fc\". Better: strip dots WITHOUT adding space (\"vitoria f. c.\" → \"vitoria fc\") then token-strip \"fc\" → \"vitoria\" ✓ + code ES ✓. So: canonical_key(base) = strip_accents lower, remove dots/dashes, collapse spaces, then strip leading/trailing club tokens.\n- \"santa cruz fc\" → santa cruz ✓ (codes PE/RN/RS ambiguous; default? bare \"Santa Cruz\" appears → unresolvable → own key \"santa cruz\" separate from santa cruz|PE etc. Add DEFAULT_CODE santa cruz → PE (the famous one). ✓\n- \"santo andre sp\"/\"Santo Andre SP\" → parses code SP ✓.\n- \"gama\"/\"gama - df\"/\"SE Gama\" → \"se gama\" → alias → gama+DF; gama codes {DF} ✓.\n- \"macae esporte fc\"/\"Macae Esporte RJ\" → (\"macae esporte\", None) codes {RJ?}: \"Macae Esporte RJ\" → base \"Macae Esporte\" code RJ ✓; \"Macae Esporte FC\" → fc stripped → macae esporte ✓ unify.\n- \"paysandu - pa\"/\"Paysandu\" ✓ unify.\n- \"internacional sc\" → alias → (\"internacional\",\"SC\"); internacional codes {RS,SC,NONE(bare)} → ambiguous; default RS for bare ✓.\n- \"atletico - es\"? \"Atletico - ES\" — Atlético Esportivo? hmm base atletico code ES — separate ✓.\n- \"atletico - ba\"? exists \"Atlético - BA\" → atletico|BA ✓.\n- \"juventude - ma\"/\"Juventude MA\" → juventude|MA ✓ (separate from Juventude-RS — there IS a \"Juventude de Mao\"? whatever, data-consistent).\n- \"criciuma - sc\" etc ✓.\n- \"flamengo - pi\" → flamengo|PI ✓ separate from flamengo (bare, RJ? wait: \"Flamengo\" bare appears (BR-Football, Libertadores, FIFA) and \"Flamengo-RJ\"/\"Flamengo - RJ\". codes {RJ, PI, NONE} → ambiguous → bare needs default RJ ✓.\n- \"fluminense de feira\" distinct ✓.\n- \"coritiba - pr\" ✓ unify {PR}.\n- \"cuiaba\" {MT, NONE} → unify → \"cuiabá\" ✓.\n- \"sport - pe\"/\"Sport-PE\"/\"Sport Recife\" aliased → sport {PE, NONE?} bare \"Sport\" exists → default PE ✓.\n- \"ponte preta - sp\" ✓.\n- \"red bull bragantino - sp\"/\"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\"/\"Red Bull Brasil - SP\"/\"Red Bull Brasil\"/\"Bragantino - SP\"/\"Bragantino - PA\"/\"Bragantino PA\" — careful! \"Bragantino - PA\" is Bragantino de Parauapebas (PA club, old name?) vs \"Bragantino - SP\" (Clube Atlético Bragantino). codes {SP, PA, NONE?}: bare \"Bragantino\" exists → ambiguous → default SP ✓. \"red bull brasil\" → alias → (\"bragantino\",\"SP\") ✓ (Red Bull Brasil became Red Bull Bragantino).\n- \"vila nova\"/\"Vila Nova - GO\" {GO} ✓; \"villa nova\"/\"Villa Nova - MG\" → base \"villa nova\" — DIFFERENT club (Villa Nova-MG)! Keys \"vila nova\" vs \"villa nova\" — distinct ✓ (phew).\n- \"nova iguacu\"/\"Nova Iguaçu - RJ\" ✓.\n- \"volta redonda\" ✓.\n- \"abc\"/\"ABC - RN\"/\"Abc - RN\" → abc {RN,NONE?} wait \"ABC\" bare exists → codes {RN, NONE} single state → unify key \"abc\" ✓.\n- \"aguia negra - ms\"/\"Aguia Negra-MS\"/'Águia Negra - MS' ✓; \"Aguia - PA\"/\"Aguia de Maraba\" — Águia de Marabá (PA): base \"aguia\" code PA; base \"aguia de maraba\" → alias → (\"aguia\",\"PA\") ✓ codes {PA} unify.\n- \"iv de julho - pi\"/\"4 de Julho - PI\" — OCR-ish \"Iv de Julho\" = \"4 de Julho\"? alias \"iv de julho\" → (\"4 de julho\",\"PI\") — cute, add.\n- \"sampaio correa\"/\"Sampaio Correa - MA\"/'Sampaio Corrêa - MA' ✓ codes {MA} unify.\n- \"tuntum ec\" → trailing \"ec\" stripped ✓ \"tuntum\".\n- Libertadores country codes: \"Guaraní (PAR)\"/\"Guaraní-PAR\" → base guarani code PAR ✓ (vs Brazilian \"Guarani - SP\" code SP, \"Guarani - CE\" CE, bare \"Guarani\" → codes {SP,CE,PAR,NONE} → bare default SP ✓; guarani|PAR separate ✓).\n- \"nacional (par)\"/\"nacional (uru)\"/\"Nacional-URU\"/\"Nacional - AM\"/\"Nacional AM\" → nacional {PAR,URU,AM,NONE}: bare \"Nacional\"? not in list? \"Nacional AM\" suffixed AM ✓. No bare → each coded ✓.\n- \"river plate\"/\"River Plate-URU\" → river plate {NONE(=ARG implied), URU} — bare stays its own \"river plate\" (ARG) — ambiguity resolution: codes excluding None = {URU} size 1 BUT None present... my rule said: if exactly one non-None code and None also present → unify (cuiabá case). That would WRONGLY merge River Plate (ARG) with River Plate-URU! Distinction: Brazilian state codes vs country codes. Refine rule: unification (drop code) applies ONLY to BR state codes; country codes ALWAYS stay in identity. And None-defaulting only for state-ambiguity. For River Plate: code URU (country) → always separate from bare (ARG) ✓. For \"Universitario (PER)\"/\"Universitario-PER\" → both PER → same club ✓. \"América de Cali\" — Colombian but no code → own club ✓ (vs \"america\" MG/RN — base differs).\n- \"barcelona-equ\" → Barcelona (EQU) ✓ separate from Barcelona (ESP, FIFA only) — base \"barcelona\" codes {EQU} for match data; FIFA \"FC Barcelona\" → key \"barcelona\"?? — FIFA club linking: \"FC Barcelona\" strips fc → \"barcelona\" no code → different from \"barcelona|EQU\" ✓ good.\n- \"delfin-equ\" ✓. \"olimpia-par\" ✓ (Olimpia bare? \"Olimpia-PAR\" only) ✓. \"libertad-par\" ✓. \"trujillanos (ven)\" ✓. \"universitario (per)\" ✓. \"tolima\"/\"Deportes Tolima\"/\"Deportivo Tolima\"?? \"Deportes Tolima\" and \"Tolima\" → different bases?! \"Tolima\" & \"Deportes Tolima\" — same club! alias \"deportes tolima\" → \"tolima\". Hmm, and FIFA \"Deportivo Toluca\"/\"Toluca\"? whatever — add alias deportes tolima → tolima.\n- \"rentistas \" trailing space — .strip() handles.\n- \"león\" vs \"León\"? one entry.\n- \"ind. santa fe\" → dots stripped → \"ind santa fe\" vs FIFA \"Independiente Santa Fe\"? not in FIFA BR list. skip.\n\nOK. The registry: two-phase.\nPhase A: for each raw team name, parse → (base, code). Apply FULL_ALIASES on canonical_key(base) → corrected (base_key, code) mapping. Store per (base_key, code).\nPhase B: resolve ambiguity per base_key: distinct state codes (BR states only, ignoring None) — if ≥2 → ambiguous; keys = base_key|code (None → default if base in DEFAULT_STATE else standalone key base_key). If exactly 1 state and None present → all unify → key = base_key (code dropped). If 1 state and no None → key = base_key. If 0 states (no codes at all) → key = base_key.\nWait subtlety: ambiguous base with None entries and no default: e.g. base \"operario\" {PR,MS,MT} + none? \"Operário - MS\" etc all coded; no bare operario. OK. Base \"santos\" {SP,AP,NONE} → default SP.\nBase \"atletico\" {AC,BA,GO,PR,MG,ES,NONE}: default? bare \"Atletico\" — appears? \"Atletico - ES\" is coded; bare \"Atletico\"? not in list I think (\"Atlético - AC\" etc all coded). \"Atletico Mineiro\"→MG alias, \"Atletico Paranaense\"→PR alias, \"Atletico Goianiense\"→GO alias. Hmm wait: \"Atlético Mineiro - MG\" parses base \"atlético mineiro\" code MG → alias on base_key \"atletico mineiro\" → (atletico, MG) ✓.\n\nNow display: per key, choose display from raw forms: prefer the most frequent accented form; for ambiguous keys append \"-CODE\". Plus DISPLAY_OVERRIDES for a few.\n\nPhase B needs all raws known → registry built after loading all files. Player clubs: register FIFA clubs in the SAME registry? Mixing FIFA international clubs (652) with match teams — fine, but FIFA-only clubs don't pollute match-team ambiguity stats if I register match teams FIRST and freeze ambiguity resolution? Simpler: two registries? Cross-file linking needs same key space. Alternative: single registry, but ambiguity resolution computed only over MATCH team names; FIFA club names then mapped via same parse+alias into that resolved key space (they're mostly full names w/o state codes, e.g. \"Atlético Mineiro\" → alias → atletico|MG ✓, \"Santos\" bare → default SP ✓, \"Bahia\" → bahia ✓, \"Cruzeiro\" → cruzeiro {MG only} ✓, \"Internacional\" → default RS ✓, \"Vitória\" → vitoria {BA,ES,NONE}→ wait FIFA \"Vitória\" bare + match data \"Vitória - BA\"/\"Vitoria ES\" → default BA ✓, \"Sport Club do Recife\" → sport|PE ✓, \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → ceara ✓, \"Chapecoense\" ✓, \"Botafogo\" → default? botafogo {PB,RJ,SP} ambiguous, bare \"Botafogo\" appears in Libertadores AND FIFA → default RJ ✓ (famous Botafogo).\n- \"Fluminense\" {RJ} ✓. \"Grêmio\" {RS} ✓. \"Paraná\" {PR, NONE}: \"Paraná - PR\",\"Parana-PR\",\"Parana\",\"CA Parana\" → alias \"ca parana\"→parana; codes {PR, NONE} unify ✓. \"Atlético Paranaense\" → atletico|PR ✓. \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → alias ✓.\n\nGreat — single registry, match teams registered first (so ambiguity stats use match data), then FIFA clubs mapped through the same alias/default logic.\n\nImplementation detail: registry.resolve(raw) → key; registry.display(key) → str. Cache per raw string.\n\n**Standings sanity:** I'll test 2019 Série A champion == Flamengo using deduped data. If data quirks break it, I'll verify with a quick script before finalizing tests. Also note: 2019 exists in Brasileirao_Matches, novo, and BR-Football Serie A → dedupe required for correct standings. Let me make dedupe priority: BR-Football first (richest stats), then Brasileirao_Matches, then novo. Hmm wait — actually is BR-Football's Serie A complete for 2014-2019? 3689 Serie A rows over 2014-2023 = ~10 seasons × 380 = 3800 — close to 3689 (missing some). Whatever — dedupe (season, home, away) across sources; union should be complete.\n\nHmm, one risk: BR-Football Serie A 2014 might have duplicate (season,home,away) vs its own rows? Checked: 0 dup keys within BR-Football by (tournament,date,home,away). But (season, home, away) without date — Copa do Brasil can have same pairing twice in a season (two different rounds!) — that's why cup dedupe uses (date, home, away). For Serie A use (season, home, away) — safe.\n\nNow what about Série A match appearing in Brasileirao_Matches 2014 and BR-Football Serie A 2014 with slightly different dates (postponed/reflection) — dedupe by (season,home,away) regardless of date ✓.\n\n**MCP e2e test:** use `mcp.shared.memory`? In mcp 1.x: `from mcp.shared.memory import create_connected_server_and_client_session` — yes exists. Test: initialize session, list_tools, call get_competitions, call search_matches.\n\nNow write the code. Also requirements.txt:\n```\nmcp>=1.29,<2\npytest\npytest-bdd\npytest-cov (already)\n```\nInstall pytest-bdd.\n\nLet me also double check FastMCP API in 1.29: FastMCP(name), @mcp.tool() decorator, @mcp.resource(\"uri://...\") — resources returning str. run via mcp.run(transport='stdio'). ✓\n\nData dir resolution: default `data/kaggle` relative to repo root (parent of package). Allow env var `SOCCER_DATA_DIR`.\n\nWrite code now. Order: normalize.py, models.py, loader.py, store.py, analytics.py (merge into store? keep separate for clarity), tools.py, server.py.\n\nActually to keep it manageable, I'll structure:\n- `brazilian_soccer/normalize.py`\n- `brazilian_soccer/models.py` (dataclasses Match, Player; competition constants)\n- `brazilian_soccer/loader.py` (CSV → objects + dedupe)\n- `brazilian_soccer/store.py` (SoccerStore: registry + indexes + all query/analytics methods; imports analytics helpers? I'll put analytics logic inside store.py as methods, keep store.py cohesive but it'll be ~450 lines. Alternatively analytics.py with functions taking store. I'll do analytics.py: functions store→results, used by store methods/tools.)\n- `brazilian_soccer/tools.py` (MCP-facing tool functions + ALL_TOOLS metadata)\n- `server.py` (FastMCP wiring, resources, main())\n\nTests:\n- tests/unit/test_normalize.py\n- tests/unit/test_loader.py\n- tests/bdd/features/*.feature (5 files)\n- tests/bdd/step_defs/*.py + conftest.py\n- tests/test_mcp_server.py (e2e)\n- tests/test_sample_questions.py (20+ questions checklist)\n\nTotal scenario count target ≥ 25.\n\nLet me write normalize.py first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ae13f8d001AGFotQwUwprZWr","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05ade4702001QFLG866QCWJXWu"}}
