{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788231262984,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_b5dc9055ab124d72b656ab0b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/normalize.py","oldString":"import re\nimport unicodedata\nfrom datetime import date, datetime","newString":"import re\nimport unicodedata\nfrom datetime import datetime"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/normalize.py\n@@ -31,9 +31,9 @@\n from __future__ import annotations\n \n import re\n import unicodedata\n-from datetime import date, datetime\n+from datetime import datetime\n \n BR_STATES = {\n     \"AC\", \"AL\", \"AP\", \"AM\", \"BA\", \"CE\", \"DF\", \"ES\", \"GO\", \"MA\", \"MT\", \"MS\",\n     \"MG\", \"PA\", \"PB\", \"PR\", \"PE\", \"PI\", \"RJ\", \"RN\", \"RS\", \"RO\", \"RR\", \"SC\",\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/normalize.py\n@@ -31,9 +31,9 @@\n from __future__ import annotations\n \n import re\n import unicodedata\n-from datetime import date, datetime\n+from datetime import datetime\n \n BR_STATES = {\n     \"AC\", \"AL\", \"AP\", \"AM\", \"BA\", \"CE\", \"DF\", \"ES\", \"GO\", \"MA\", \"MT\", \"MS\",\n     \"MG\", \"PA\", \"PB\", \"PR\", \"PE\", \"PI\", \"RJ\", \"RN\", \"RS\", \"RO\", \"RR\", \"SC\",\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788231262981,"end":1788231262983}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There are a few issues to fix in my written file:\n\n1. `_ACCENT_TABLE` is unused junk — remove.\n2. `_CLUB_TOKENS` includes \"ca\" — that would strip \"CA\" from \"CA Parana\" → \"parana\"... wait that's actually what I want for \"CA Parana\" → but I also have explicit alias. But \"ca\" stripping is dangerous: \"Caucaia\" is one token \"caucaia\" — not stripped (token-based). Only exact tokens stripped: \"ca\" alone. Any club named \"CA\"? No. OK but \"Caracas\"? one token. Fine. Actually danger: \"ABC\" is one token \"abc\" not in set. Fine. But what about \"Gama AC\"? → \"gama\" ✓. Hmm \"AC\" stripping: \"Rio Branco AC\" → \"rio branco\" — Rio Branco-AC → code AC parsed first by regex! parse_team_name handles \"Rio Branco AC\" → base \"Rio Branco\", code AC (state). Then canonical_key(\"Rio Branco\") → \"rio branco\". OK.\n   BUT the token-strip of \"ac\" affects bases like \"Rio Branco AC\" if regex didn't match... fine.\n   Danger case: \"CRAC\" — one token, fine. \"Galvez AC\" → regex parses code AC ✓.\n3. The `_pick_display` rank function: `self._has_accent(name)` returns bool — max() with tuple ranks: bool True > False — prefers accented ✓.\n4. Problem: `register()` returns provisional key but caches raw→provisional. Then `finalize()` recomputes final_cache — good. But `key_for` after finalize: `register()` would re-add variants — fine since cache hit.\n5. Issue in `finalize()`: `disp = DISPLAY_OVERRIDES.get(key) or self._display.get(key)` — `_display.get(key)` is always None at that point (key just being set). Remove that leftover.\n6. `_pick_display` for unambiguous base (key = base_key): code may be non-None (e.g. \"cuiaba\" with code MT and bare) — states = {MT} size 1 → no suffix appended → display \"Cuiabá\" ✓. For base with code=None only → display bare ✓.\n7. Issue: two different (base_key, code) variants mapping to the SAME final key (e.g. unambiguous base: (\"cuiaba\", None) and (\"cuiaba\", \"MT\") both → key \"cuiaba\"). `_display[key]` computed twice — second call overwrites with the other variant's display. Both compute the same base name anyway (both count their own raws). Mostly fine — but for consistency, accumulate display candidates per final key. Minor; overwrite is acceptable since same base name. Edge: (\"internacional\", None) raws [\"Internacional\", \"Internacional RS\"?? no that has code RS]. fine.\n8. Another subtlety: parse_team_name regex `^(?P<base>.*?)[\\s\\-–—]+\\(?(?P<code>[A-Z]{2,3})\\)?\\s*$` with non-greedy base — on \"Palmeiras-SP\": base \"Palmeiras\" code SP ✓. On \"America MG\": base \"America\" ✓. On \"ASA AL\": base \"ASA\" ✓. On \"Nacional (URU)\": base \"Nacional\" ✓. On \"Rentistas\" (no code) → no match → base \"Rentistas\" ✓. On \"ABC\": does regex match \"ABC\" as code with base \"\"? base `.*?` non-greedy empty, then `[\\s\\-–—]+` requires at least one separator char — \"ABC\" has no separator → no match ✓. On \"CENE MS\": base \"CENE\" code MS ✓. On \"Santos - AP\": base \"Santos\" ✓. On \"Aguia Negra-MS\": ✓. On \"7 de Setembro - MS\" ✓. On \"Botafogo PB\": base \"Botafogo\" code PB ✓. On \"4 de Julho - PI\" ✓. On \"Vitoria F. C. - ES\": base \"Vitoria F. C.\" code ES ✓. On \"Rio Branco - Vn - ES\": regex non-greedy — `.*?` matches minimal... The match must end at \"$\", code \"ES\". Base: \"Rio Branco - Vn - \" stripped → \"Rio Branco - Vn\"? Hmm non-greedy `.*?` tries shortest: base \"Rio Branco\", separator \" - \", code... \"Vn\" is not [A-Z]{2,3} (Vn has lowercase n) → backtrack → base grows until code \"ES\" ✓ base \"Rio Branco - Vn\". canonical_key → \"rio branco vn\" — separate club from \"rio branco\". Eh — Rio Branco de Varginha? it's \"Rio Branco-VN\" (Venda Nova?) — ES state. It'd be its own club \"rio branco vn\". Acceptable (it IS a different club from Rio Branco-AC). OK.\n9. `_CODE_AT_END` on \"Juazeiro - BA\" ✓. On \"Treze - PB\" ✓.\n10. Wait — problem: regex requires separator `[\\s\\-–—]+` — for \"Barcelona-EQU\" ✓ code EQU.\n11. \"Universitario (PER)\" — paren annotation removal: `\\((?!\\s*[A-Z]{2,3}\\s*\\))[^)]*\\)` — \"(PER)\" IS a bare code (PER matches [A-Z]{2,3}) → NOT removed → then regex parses code PER ✓.\n12. \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\": annotation regex — \"(antigo...\" doesn't start with 2-3 caps → removed → \"Boavista Sport Club  - RJ\" → base \"Boavista Sport Club\" code RJ ✓ → alias \"boavista sport club\" → (\"boavista\",\"RJ\") ✓.\n\n13. One more: canonical_key strips leading/trailing club tokens — \"ca\" token: \"CA Parana\" → parse base \"CA Parana\"? wait no: \"CA Parana\" has no trailing code → base \"CA Parana\" → canonical_key: \"ca parana\" → strip leading \"ca\" → \"parana\" ✓ alias unnecessary but harmless.\n\n14. Danger: canonical_key strips trailing \"cf\": \"SC Corinthians Paulista\"? doesn't appear in data. fine.\n\n15. Issue: `_pick_display` — when key has DISPLAY_OVERRIDES we skip. When unambiguous base key like \"river\" → override \"Ríver-PI\" ✓.\n\n16. Bug in finalize: for COUNTRY_CODES with bare variant (e.g. \"river plate\" bare → key \"river plate\", code None → `code in COUNTRY_CODES` False → len(states)>=2? states = BR states only = {} → len 0 → key = \"river plate\" ✓ separate from \"river plate|URU\" ✓ good.\n\n17. Bug: `_pick_display(base_key, code, raws)` for key \"river plate\" (code None) — counts include raw \"River Plate\" ✓.\n\nNow — one design flaw: `register()` called during load returns provisional keys; matches store keys; finalize() must rewrite keys in matches. Instead, cleaner: loader collects raw names first, finalizes registry, THEN creates Match objects using registry.key_for(raw). I'll structure loader accordingly: pass 1 read CSV rows → intermediate dicts; collect team names; registry.finalize(); pass 2 map to Match objects. \n\nAlso `display()` fallback returns key itself — fine.\n\nAlso remove unused `date` import, `_ACCENT_TABLE`. And `keys()` returns sorted display keys. Let me clean up.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ae3a2f8001Y5M0221RXL7ixT","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05ae2d552001pUH73QVUElldj7"}}
