``python\n@dataclass Match:\n    competition: str        # canonical: \"Brasileirão Serie A\" | \"Brasileirão Serie B\" | \"Brasileirão Serie C\" | \"Copa do Brasil\" | \"Copa Libertadores\"\n    season: int\n    date: date | None\n    time: str | None\n    round: int | None       # league round / cup round number\n    stage: str | None       # \"final\", \"semifinals\", \"group stage\", ... (Libertadores given; derived for cup)\n    home_key, away_key\n    home_display, away_display\n    home_goal, away_goal: int | None\n    source: str             # dataset file stem\n    # optional extended stats:\n    home_corner, away_corner, home_shots, away_shots, home_attack, away_attack, total_corners\n    arena: str | None\n    home_state, away_state: str | None\n    \n@dataclass Player:\n    id, name, age, nationality, overall, potential, club_key, club_display, club_raw, position, jersey, height, weight, value, wage, skills dict\n```\n\nloader.py: functions to load each CSV into intermediate dicts, then build Matches + registry. Competition mapping:\n- Brasileirao_Matches.csv → \"Brasileirão Serie A\", source \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\"\n- Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv → \"Copa do Brasil\"\n- Libertadores_Matches.csv → \"Copa Libertadores\"\n- BR-Football-Dataset.csv → map tournament: \"Serie A\" → \"Brasileirão Serie A\", \"Serie B\" → \"Brasileirão Serie B\", \"Serie C\" → \"Brasileirão Serie C\", \"Copa do Brasil\" → \"Copa do Brasil\"\n- novo → \"Brasileirão Serie A\"\n- fifa → players\n\nCompetition family for dedupe: {\"brasileirao serie a\", \"brasileirao serie b\", \"brasileirao serie c\"} → dedupe key (competition, season, home_key, away_key); \"copa do brasil\" → (competition, date, home_key, away_key); libertadores → none.\n\nPriority: BR-Football (source rank 0, richest) > Brasileirao_Matches (1) > novo (2). For cup: BR-Football > Brazilian_Cup_Matches. Hmm — cup: BR-Football has corners etc. ✓.\n\nWait — actually think about which source to prefer for Série A: BR-Football Serie A 2014-2023 — does it have all 380 matches per season? 3689 rows / 10 seasons ≈ 369/season — roughly complete. Its team names lack accents (\"Sao Paulo\") — display resolution handles via registry. But BR-Football has no round numbers! Keeping BR-Football rows drops round info for 2014-2019 Série A. Hmm — that's a data-quality tradeoff. Priority matters for correctness of standings? No — standings computed from results; any source equivalent. Round info is nice for display (\"Brasileirão Round 22\" in example). \n\nReconsider: prefer Brasileirao_Matches (has round + states) for Série A, novo as second (has arena, round), BR-Football third? But BR-Football is the ONLY source of 2023 Série A — still included when others absent. For 2014-2019: Brasileirao_Matches wins, keeping rounds. novo vs Brasileirao_Matches overlap 2012-2019: both have rounds; Brasileirao_Matches has state suffixes; novo has arena. Pick Brasileirao_Matches (its team names include states which the spec calls out; also 4180-row file is the primary dataset named in the spec). Order: Brasileirao_Matches (1) > novo (2) > BR-Football (3) for Serie A/B/C; for Copa do Brasil: Brazilian_Cup_Matches (has round!) > BR-Football. Cup round info matters for finals. And BR-Football cup rows lack rounds. ✓.\n\nHmm wait — but then the \"extended stats\" (corners/shots) from BR-Football are lost for overlapping matches. Acceptable: extended stats only for non-overlapping matches (2022-2023 Série A, 2022-2023 cups, all Série B/C). Fine — provenance preserved.\n\nActually, hmm, one more consideration: rather than rank-dropping, I could MERGE (fill missing round from other source). Overkill. Keep rank-based.\n\nDedupe detail: novo has 1 internal dup — caught by dedupe (same key, rank 2, first kept).\n\nSeason for BR-Football = date.year. For \"Copa do Brasil\" spanning years (e.g. 2023 final in Sept — same year; some editions span two years? 2014-2023 data seems single-year). Use year.\n\nRound/stage for cup: derive stage: round == max round within season → \"final\"; round == max-1 → \"semifinals\"? Hmm Brazilian Cup had semifinals before final ✓. round == max-2 → \"quarterfinals\". Only label final explicitly; else f\"round {round}\". Keep stage=None for league.\n\nWait — cup rounds 1..8: 2012 Copa do Brasil had 8 rounds? Actually the dataset shows rounds 1-8 — but Copa do Brasil from 2013 has 7 rounds (with preliminary?). Per-season max works regardless.\n\nPlayers: fifa_data.csv columns — need to check exact names: 'ID','Name','Age','Photo','Nationality','Flag','Overall','Potential','Club','Club Logo','Value','Wage','Special','Preferred Foot','International Reputation','Weak Foot','Skill Moves','Work Rate','Body Type','Real Face','Position','Jersey Number','Joined','Loaned From','Contract Valid Until','Height','Weight', then position slots (LS..RB), then skills: Crossing, Finishing, HeadingAccuracy, ShortPassing, Volleys, Dribbling, Curve, FKAccuracy, LongPassing, BallControl, Acceleration, SprintSpeed, Agility, Reactions, Balance, ShotPower, Jumping, Stamina, Strength, LongShots, Aggression, Interceptions, Positioning, Vision, Penalties, Composure, Marking, StandingTackle, SlidingTackle, GKDiving, GKHandling, GKKicking, GKPositioning, GKReflexes. Let me verify exact header list.\n\nThen store.py + analytics. Let me write models.py now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05aed96e600122mAn08WJ2BDwS","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05aece7ff001WoEuz1lpCmq27c"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1788231915591,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"id":"prt_05aed9845001ydUebi9JhuIE26","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"a829eb1c88c4370fa327cf9bb6616213ad7fbe78","messageID":"msg_05aece7ff001WoEuz1lpCmq27c","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":151216,"input":3991,"output":50,"reasoning":1447,"cache":{"write":0,"read":145728}},"cost":0.002859495}}
