{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788232384880,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_5887f862d7bf4fd686d13ab8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py","newString":"def _cup_stage(round_no: int | None, max_round: int | None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Derive a friendly stage label for cup matches.\"\"\"\n    if round_no is None or max_round is None:\n        return None\n    if round_no == max_round:\n        return \"final\"\n    if round_no == max_round - 1:\n        return \"semifinals\"\n    if round_no == max_round - 2:\n        return \"quarterfinals\"\n    return f\"round {round_no}\"\n\n\ndef _team(registry: TeamRegistry, raw: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Register a raw team name for identity resolution; keep the raw form.\"\"\"\n    registry.register(raw)\n    return raw","oldString":"def _cup_stage(round_no: int | None, max_round: int | None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Derive a friendly stage label for cup matches.\"\"\"\n    if round_no is None or max_round is None:\n        return None\n    if round_no == max_round:\n        return \"final\"\n    if round_no == max_round - 1:\n        return \"semifinals\"\n    if round_no == max_round - 2:\n        return \"quarterfinals\"\n    return f\"round {round_no}\""},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -82,8 +82,14 @@\n         return \"quarterfinals\"\n     return f\"round {round_no}\"\n \n \n+def _team(registry: TeamRegistry, raw: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Register a raw team name for identity resolution; keep the raw form.\"\"\"\n+    registry.register(raw)\n+    return raw\n+\n+\n def load_match_rows(registry: TeamRegistry) -> list[Match]:\n     \"\"\"Load all match datasets into normalized Match objects.\n \n     Team identity: ``home_raw``/``away_raw`` store the raw names; canonical\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -82,8 +82,14 @@\n         return \"quarterfinals\"\n     return f\"round {round_no}\"\n \n \n+def _team(registry: TeamRegistry, raw: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Register a raw team name for identity resolution; keep the raw form.\"\"\"\n+    registry.register(raw)\n+    return raw\n+\n+\n def load_match_rows(registry: TeamRegistry) -> list[Match]:\n     \"\"\"Load all match datasets into normalized Match objects.\n \n     Team identity: ``home_raw``/``away_raw`` store the raw names; canonical\n","additions":6,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/loader.py","time":{"start":1788232384878,"end":1788232384879}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"`variants: 0` after load_match_rows! The registry registered NOTHING. But matches loaded (rows > 0 presumably). So `registry.register(...)` inside loader didn't populate `reg._variants`...\n\nIn loader.load_match_rows I call `registry.register(r[\"home_team\"])` — wait, do I? Let me check the current loader code... I REWROTE loader to store `home_raw=r[\"home_team\"]` — and register calls were REMOVED! I removed the `home_key=registry.register(...)` lines and never added explicit `registry.register(...)` calls! So nothing gets registered.\n\nFix: in load_match_rows, explicitly register raw names (I can ignore return values), OR rely on load_all calling register via key_for AFTER finalize — but that breaks \"ambiguity judged on match data only\" ordering.\n\nAdd explicit registration at the start of each row loop (or a helper `_reg(registry, name)` returning raw). Cleanest: in each row construction, call `registry.register(name)` and store the raw string:\n\n```python\ndef _team(registry, raw):\n    registry.register(raw)\n    return raw\n```\nThen `home_raw=_team(registry, r[\"home_team\"])`.\n\nAlso fix Libertadores season 0 (1 row): fallback to date.year. In loader: `season=parse_int(r[\"season\"]) or (d.year if d else 0)` — need to parse date first for Libertadores. Restructure that block: parse date first.\n\nAnd then re-check Série A 2019 = 343 issue — which might resolve... no wait, it won't: dedupe happened with EMPTY keys — every match key (\"league\", comp, season, \"\", \"\")?? NO — dedupe key uses m.home_key which was \"\" for all rows (never assigned)! So ALL Série A 2019 matches collapsed to ONE key → 343... no wait, one key → 1 match. We got 343 for 2019 — hmm. With empty home_key/away_key, key = (\"league\", comp, season, \"\", \"\") — ALL 2019 Série A matches share ONE key → best kept = 1 match. But we saw 343?? That was after load_all assigned keys — no wait, load_all assigns keys AFTER dedupe in the buggy order? Current code: finalize → assign keys to match_rows → dedupe(match_rows). Order in current file: registry.finalize(); assign keys for m in match_rows; matches = dedupe_matches(match_rows). ✓ so keys WERE assigned (via key_for — which registers post-finalize lazily... key_for with finalized=True computes key from parsed name — works even if register never called (states set from _variants — EMPTY since nothing registered!). states = {} for everything → len(states)>=2 False → key = base_key — no state distinction! So \"Internacional - SC\" → \"internacional\" == \"Internacional\" bare → merged. THAT's why 2019 got 343 (over-merged pairs like atletico|MG vs atletico|GO collisions? no... e.g. \"Juventude-RS\" vs \"Juventude - MA\" both → \"juventude\" → their matches collided on dedupe keys and stats).\n\nSo the ROOT FIX is: register all names during load_match_rows (before finalize). Then everything downstream works.\n\nLet me apply both fixes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05af4c15d0012AygPM147JYU7p","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05af43e54001fFti2EyEhxp7ll"}}
