{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788233020494,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_a7f43d40285848cea17a3abb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Statistical computations over normalized Match objects.\n\nAll functions are pure: they take lists of already-filtered matches (and\ncanonical team keys) and return plain dictionaries, ready to be serialized\nby the MCP tool layer.\n\nLeague standings assume a double round-robin (3 points per win, 1 per\ndraw) with the classic tiebreak order: points, wins, goal difference,\ngoals scored.  The 2019 Série A season computed from the union of the\nthree overlapping datasets reproduces exactly 380 matches and Flamengo as\nchampion, which the BDD suite asserts as a data-quality gate.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nfrom .models import LEAGUE_COMPETITIONS, Match\n\n\ndef team_record(matches: list[Match], key: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Win/draw/loss record of one team across the given matches.\"\"\"\n    rec = {\"matches\": 0, \"wins\": 0, \"draws\": 0, \"losses\": 0,\n           \"goals_for\": 0, \"goals_against\": 0}\n    for m in matches:\n        if not m.has_result() or key not in (m.home_key, m.away_key):\n            continue\n        rec[\"matches\"] += 1\n        gf = m.home_goal if m.home_key == key else m.away_goal\n        ga = m.away_goal if m.home_key == key else m.home_goal\n        rec[\"goals_for\"] += gf\n        rec[\"goals_against\"] += ga\n        if gf > ga:\n            rec[\"wins\"] += 1\n        elif gf < ga:\n            rec[\"losses\"] += 1\n        else:\n            rec[\"draws\"] += 1\n    rec[\"points\"] = rec[\"wins\"] * 3 + rec[\"draws\"]\n    total = rec[\"wins\"] + rec[\"draws\"] + rec[\"losses\"]\n    rec[\"win_rate\"] = round(100.0 * rec[\"wins\"] / total, 1) if total else 0.0\n    return rec\n\n\ndef h2h_record(matches: list[Match], team_a: str, team_b: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Head-to-head summary between two canonical keys.\"\"\"\n    rec = {team_a: 0, team_b: 0, \"draws\": 0}\n    goals = {team_a: 0, team_b: 0}\n    for m in matches:\n        if not m.has_result():\n            continue\n        if m.home_key == team_a and m.away_key == team_b:\n            goals[team_a] += m.home_goal\n            goals[team_b] += m.away_goal\n        elif m.home_key == team_b and m.away_key == team_a:\n            goals[team_b] += m.home_goal\n            goals[team_a] += m.away_goal\n        else:\n            continue\n        w = m.winner_key()\n        if w is None:\n            rec[\"draws\"] += 1\n        else:\n            rec[w] += 1\n    return {\n        \"team_a_wins\": rec[team_a],\n        \"team_b_wins\": rec[team_b],\n        \"draws\": rec[\"draws\"],\n        \"team_a_goals\": goals[team_a],\n        \"team_b_goals\": goals[team_b],\n    }\n\n\ndef standings_table(matches: list[Match]) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"League table from a season's matches (double round-robin).\"\"\"\n    rows: dict[str, dict] = {}\n    for m in matches:\n        if not m.has_result():\n            continue\n        for key, gf, ga in ((m.home_key, m.home_goal, m.away_goal),\n                            (m.away_key, m.away_goal, m.home_goal)):\n            row = rows.setdefault(key, {\n                \"team\": key, \"matches\": 0, \"wins\": 0, \"draws\": 0,\n                \"losses\": 0, \"goals_for\": 0, \"goals_against\": 0,\n            })\n            row[\"matches\"] += 1\n            row[\"goals_for\"] += gf\n            row[\"goals_against\"] += ga\n            if gf > ga:\n                row[\"wins\"] += 1\n            elif gf < ga:\n                row[\"losses\"] += 1\n            else:\n                row[\"draws\"] += 1\n    table = []\n    for r in rows.values():\n        r[\"goal_difference\"] = r[\"goals_for\"] - r[\"goals_against\"]\n        r[\"points\"] = r[\"wins\"] * 3 + r[\"draws\"]\n        table.append(r)\n    table.sort(key=lambda r: (-r[\"points\"], -r[\"wins\"], -r[\"goal_difference\"],\n                              -r[\"goals_for\"], r[\"team\"]))\n    for i, r in enumerate(table, start=1):\n        r[\"position\"] = i\n    return table\n\n\ndef biggest_wins(matches: list[Match], top: int = 10) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Matches with the largest goal margin (winning side first).\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for m in matches:\n        if not m.has_result():\n            continue\n        margin = abs(m.home_goal - m.away_goal)\n        if margin == 0:\n            continue\n        if m.home_goal > m.away_goal:\n            winner, loser, wf, lf = m.home_key, m.away_key, m.home_goal, m.away_goal\n        else:\n            winner, loser, wf, lf = m.away_key, m.home_key, m.away_goal, m.home_goal\n        out.append({\"margin\": margin, \"winner\": winner, \"loser\": loser,\n                    \"winner_goals\": wf, \"loser_goals\": lf, \"match\": m})\n    out.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[\"margin\"], x[\"match\"].date or __import__(\"datetime\").date.min))\n    return out[:top]\n\n\ndef aggregate_stats(matches: list[Match]) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Average goals and home-advantage numbers for a set of matches.\"\"\"\n    played = [m for m in matches if m.has_result()]\n    total = len(played)\n    goals = sum(m.home_goal + m.away_goal for m in played)\n    home_wins = sum(1 for m in played if m.home_goal > m.away_goal)\n    away_wins = sum(1 for m in played if m.away_goal > m.home_goal)\n    draws = total - home_wins - away_wins\n    return {\n        \"matches\": total,\n        \"goals\": goals,\n        \"avg_goals_per_match\": round(goals / total, 2) if total else 0.0,\n        \"home_wins\": home_wins,\n        \"away_wins\": away_wins,\n        \"draws\": draws,\n        \"home_win_rate\": round(100.0 * home_wins / total, 1) if total else 0.0,\n        \"away_win_rate\": round(100.0 * away_wins / total, 1) if total else 0.0,\n        \"draw_rate\": round(100.0 * draws / total, 1) if total else 0.0,\n    }\n\n\ndef best_venues(matches: list[Match], venue: str, top: int = 5,\n                min_matches: int = 30) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Teams with the best home ('home') or away ('away') record.\"\"\"\n    per_team: dict[str, list[Match]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for m in matches:\n        if venue == \"home\":\n            per_team[m.home_key].append(m)\n        else:\n            per_team[m.away_key].append(m)\n    scored = []\n    for key, ms in per_team.items():\n        if len(ms) < min_matches:\n            continue\n        rec = team_record(ms, key)\n        scored.append({\"team\": key, \"record\": rec})\n    scored.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[\"record\"][\"win_rate\"], -x[\"record\"][\"wins\"]))\n    return scored[:top]\n\n\ndef season_comparison(matches_by_season: dict[int, list[Match]]) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Compare aggregate statistics across seasons.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for season in sorted(matches_by_season):\n        stats = aggregate_stats(matches_by_season[season])\n        stats[\"season\"] = season\n        out.append(stats)\n    return out\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/analytics.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/analytics.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/analytics.py","time":{"start":1788233020482,"end":1788233020491}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Everything is clean now:\n- Série A seasons: exactly 380 matches, 20 teams × 38 ✓\n- Fla-Flu: 44 matches\n- Neymar → \"Paris Saint-Germain\" ✓\n- Load: 0.64s ✓ (well under 2s)\n\nNow build the store (indexes + queries) and analytics. Let me write store.py with the SoccerStore class and analytics.py with computation functions.\n\n**store.py design:**\n\n```python\nclass SoccerStore:\n    def __init__(self, data_dir=None):  # loads via loader with DATA_DIR patched? \n```\nHmm — loader uses module-level DATA_DIR. For flexibility, make loader functions accept data_dir param with default. Simpler: SoccerStore(data_dir: Path | None) — pass to load functions. Let me refactor loader functions to take `data_dir: Path = DATA_DIR`. read_csv(path) already takes path. I'll add data_dir param to load_match_rows/load_players/load_all.\n\nStore fields:\n- registry, matches, players\n- matches_by_team: dict[str, list[Match]] (both home & away)\n- by_comp_season: dict[(comp, season), list[Match]]\n- players_by_club: dict[str, list[Player]]\n- players_by_name sorted index; normalized name tokens for search\n- competition catalog: dict comp → set seasons + counts\n- derbies table\n\nResolution of team/competition fuzzy input:\n- resolve_team(name) → key (registry.key_for handles raw names; also try display match: if user passes \"Flamengo\" ✓; \"Palmeiras-SP\" ✓)\n- resolve_competition(text) → canonical label via accent-stripped contains/aliases: \"brasileirao\"/\"serie a\"/\"brasileirao serie a\" → BRASILEIRAO_A; \"serie b\", \"serie c\", \"copa do brasil\"/\"copa do brasil\"/\"brazilian cup\", \"libertadores\"/\"copa libertadores\".\n\nMethods (called by tools):\n- search_matches(team=None, opponent=None, competition=None, season=None, stage=None, date_from=None, date_to=None, limit=25) → list[dict] + total count\n- head_to_head(team_a, team_b, competition=None) → summary + matches\n- team_stats(team, season=None, competition=None, venue=None) → record\n- standings(competition, season, top=None)\n- search_players(name=None, nationality=None, club=None, position=None, min_overall=None, max_overall=None, limit=25, brazilian_only=False)\n- get_player(name) → best match\n- competitions() → catalog\n- statistics(competition=None, season=None) → aggregates + biggest wins + best records\n- derbies(season=None, competition=None)\n- team_history(team) → per-competition per-season participation + record\n- answer_question(text) → router\n\nanalytics.py: pure functions:\n- standings_table(matches) → rows sorted\n- h2h_record(matches, a, b)\n- team_record(matches, key) → w/d/l/gf/ga\n- biggest_wins(matches, top)\n- best_home_away(matches, min_matches)\n- average_goals etc.\n\nFormatting dates: ISO strings.\n\nDerbies list (canonical key pairs) — use base keys with state where needed: flamengo|RJ vs fluminense|RJ (Fla-Flu), flamengo|RJ vs vasco|RJ (Clássico dos Milhões), flamengo|RJ vs botafogo|RJ (Clássico da Rivalidade), botafogo|RJ vs fluminense|RJ (Trio? \"Clássico Vovô\" is botafogo×fluminense — actually Clássico Vovô = Botafogo × Fluminense; Botafogo × Flamengo = \"Clássico da Rivalidade\"), Corinthians × Palmeiras (Dérbi Paulista), Corinthians × São Paulo (Majestoso), Palmeiras × São Paulo (Choque-Rei), Grêmio × Internacional (Grenal), Athletico-PR × Coritiba (Atletiba), Bahia × Vitória (Ba-Vi), Santos × São Paulo (San-São? \"Clássico San-São\" = Santos × São Paulo ✓), Santos × Corinthians? (Alvinegro... skip), Atlético-MG × Cruzeiro (Clássico Mineiro), Atlético-MG × América-MG? skip, Flamengo × Vasco done, Fluminense × Vasco? (skip), Goiás × Vila Nova (Clássico do Sudeste? no — \"Clássico dos Avós\"? hmm Goiás×Vila Nova = Clássico dos Avós? not sure — skip), Santa Cruz × Náutico × Sport (Clássico das Multidões = Sport × Santa Cruz; Clássico Emoção = Náutico × Sport?) — add Sport × Náutico (Clássico Emoção) and Sport × Santa Cruz (Clássico das Multidões), Ceará × Fortaleza (Clássico-Rei), Coritiba... enough: I'll define ~14 rivalries with names.\n\nSince keys resolve at runtime, derby definitions reference canonical keys via strings like (\"Flamengo-RJ\", \"Fluminense-RJ\") resolved through registry at store init.\n\nNow — standings tiebreak & champion: for Brasileirão. Points: W=3, D=1. Sort: pts, wins, gd, gf, then name. Champion = first. Relegation = last 4 (Série A 20 teams; but data coverage may vary — label as \"bottom 4 (relegation zone, assuming 20-team league)\").\n\n**answer_question router**: simple keyword logic:\n- contains \"vs\"/\" x \"/\" against \" + two known teams → h2h\n- \"standings\"/\"table\"/\"won the\"/\"champion\"/\"relegated\" + season + competition → standings\n- player hints (\"who is\", \"players\", \"rating\", \"overall\") → player search\n- \"derby\"/\"rivalry\" → derbies\n- \"biggest win\"/\"average goals\"/\"best home\"/\"best away\"/\"home record\"/\"away record\" → statistics\n- team stats patterns (\"record\", \"wins\") + team → team_stats\n- fallback → search_matches with extracted team names + season/year\nReturn {tool_used, answer}. Keep it modest and tested on the spec's sample questions.\n\nActually — the spec says the MCP server is connected to an LLM that does query processing via tools; the NL router is a bonus for demo/no-LLM use. I'll implement `answer_question` as a deterministic best-effort router and TEST it with the 20 sample questions from the spec (non-empty, structured responses). This directly satisfies \"At least 20 sample questions can be answered\".\n\nNow write analytics.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05afe7439001LimUDYeg4zYEAs","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05afa75f10013ebAggyVcVguos"}}
