{"type":"text","timestamp":1788233312883,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"id":"prt_05b026d24001gGJC82ydKCsXJS","messageID":"msg_05b020235001friJqQWgt5FjhH","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","type":"text","text":"All analytics verified against real-world facts (2019: Flamengo 90pts, correct relegation, 2018 Lib final, 2020 cup final). Now the MCP layer — the natural-language router and the server:","time":{"start":1788233280804,"end":1788233312880}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788233312887,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_288973fa506243f2948bc191","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"MCP tool layer: natural-language router + tool implementations.\n\nThe MCP server exposes structured tools (see ``server.py``); an LLM client\nis expected to choose the right tool and parameters.  ``answer_question``\nadditionally provides a deterministic best-effort router so simple\nquestions can be answered without an LLM: it detects years, team names,\ncompetition words and intent keywords, and dispatches to the matching\n``SoccerStore`` method.\n\nRouter intent order (first match wins):\n1. head-to-head   - two team names + \"vs\"/\"against\"/\"x\"\n2. standings      - \"standings\"/\"table\"/\"champion\"/\"won\"/\"relegated\" + year\n3. derbies        - \"derby\"/\"rivalry\"/\"clássico\"\n4. players        - \"player\"/\"who is\"/\"rating\"/\"squad\"\n5. statistics     - \"average goals\"/\"biggest win\"/\"best home\"/\"best away\"\n6. team stats     - \"record\"/\"wins\" + one team\n7. matches        - fallback: match search with detected teams/season\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\n\nfrom .normalize import strip_accents\nfrom .store import NotFound, SoccerStore\n\n_YEAR_RE = re.compile(r\"\\b(19|20)\\d{2}\\b\")\n\n\ndef _detect_years(question: str) -> list[int]:\n    return [int(y) for y in _YEAR_RE.findall(question)]\n\n\ndef _detect_teams(store: SoccerStore, question: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Find team mentions by scanning display names (longest first).\"\"\"\n    q = strip_accents(question).lower()\n    found: list[tuple[int, str]] = []\n    for key, display in store.registry.display_names().items():\n        d = strip_accents(display).lower()\n        if len(d) < 4:\n            continue\n        idx = q.find(d)\n        if idx >= 0:\n            found.append((idx, display))\n    # Longest display name at each position wins; keep reading order.\n    found.sort(key=lambda t: (t[0], -len(t[1])))\n    picked: list[str] = []\n    last_end = -1\n    for idx, display in found:\n        if idx >= last_end:\n            picked.append(display)\n            last_end = idx + len(display)\n        if len(picked) == 2:\n            break\n    return picked\n\n\ndef _detect_competition(store: SoccerStore, question: str) -> str | None:\n    q = strip_accents(question).lower()\n    if \"libertadores\" in q:\n        return \"Copa Libertadores\"\n    if \"copa do brasil\" in q or \"brazilian cup\" in q:\n        return \"Copa do Brasil\"\n    if \"serie b\" in q:\n        return \"Brasileirão Serie B\"\n    if \"serie c\" in q:\n        return \"Brasileirão Serie C\"\n    if \"serie a\" in q or \"brasileirao\" in q or \"brasileirão\" in q:\n        return \"Brasileirão Serie A\"\n    return None\n\n\ndef answer_question(store: SoccerStore, question: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort deterministic routing of a natural-language question.\"\"\"\n    q = strip_accents(question).lower()\n    years = _detect_years(question)\n    year = years[-1] if years else None\n    competition = _detect_competition(store, question)\n    teams = _detect_teams(store, question)\n\n    # 1. head-to-head\n    if len(teams) == 2 and any(w in q for w in (\" vs \", \" x \", \" against\", \" head-to-head\", \" head to head\")):\n        return {\"tool\": \"get_head_to_head\",\n                \"result\": store.head_to_head(teams[0], teams[1], competition)}\n\n    # 2. standings / champion / relegation\n    if any(w in q for w in (\"standings\", \"table\", \"champion\", \" who won\",\n                            \"relegat\", \"won the\")):\n        comp = competition or \"Brasileirão Serie A\"\n        if year is None:\n            raise NotFound(\"Which season (year)? e.g. 'Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?'\")\n        result = store.standings(comp, year, top=6)\n        if \"relegat\" in q:\n            result = {\"relegation_zone\": result.get(\"relegation_zone\")}\n        elif any(w in q for w in (\"who won\", \"champion\")):\n            result = {\"champion\": result[\"champion\"]}\n        return {\"tool\": \"get_standings\", \"result\": result}\n\n    # 3. derbies\n    if any(w in q for w in (\"derby\", \"derbies\", \"rivalry\", \"classico\", \"clássico\")):\n        return {\"tool\": \"get_derbies\",\n                \"result\": store.derbies(season=year, competition=competition)}\n\n    # 4. players\n    if any(w in q for w in (\"player\", \"who is\", \"rating\", \"overall\", \"squad\", \"forwards\")):\n        if len(teams) == 1:\n            return {\"tool\": \"search_players_at_club\",\n                    \"result\": store.players_at_club(teams[0])}\n        if \"brazil\" in q:\n            return {\"tool\": \"search_players\",\n                    \"result\": store.search_players(nationality=\"brazil\",\n                                                   min_overall=75, limit=10)}\n        return {\"tool\": \"search_players\",\n                \"result\": store.search_players(name=question, limit=5)}\n\n    # 5. statistics\n    if any(w in q for w in (\"average goals\", \"goals per match\", \"biggest win\",\n                            \"best home\", \"best away\", \"home win\")):\n        return {\"tool\": \"get_statistics\",\n                \"result\": store.statistics(competition=competition, season=year)}\n\n    # 6. team stats\n    if len(teams) == 1 and any(w in q for w in (\"record\", \"wins\", \"won how\", \"how many\")):\n        venue = None\n        if \"home\" in q:\n            venue = \"home\"\n        elif \"away\" in q:\n            venue = \"away\"\n        return {\"tool\": \"get_team_stats\",\n                \"result\": store.team_stats(teams[0], season=year,\n                                           competition=competition, venue=venue)}\n\n    # 7. match search fallback\n    if teams:\n        kwargs = {\"team\": teams[0]}\n        if len(teams) == 2:\n            kwargs[\"opponent\"] = teams[1]\n        if year:\n            kwargs[\"season\"] = year\n        if competition:\n            kwargs[\"competition\"] = competition\n        if \"last\" in q or \"when did\" in q:\n            kwargs[\"limit\"] = 5\n        return {\"tool\": \"search_matches\", \"result\": store.search_matches(**kwargs)}\n\n    raise NotFound(\n        \"Could not route the question. Structured tools are available for \"\n        \"match search, head-to-head, team stats, standings, players, \"\n        \"statistics and derbies.\")\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/tools.py","time":{"start":1788233312877,"end":1788233312885}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All analytics check out against real-world facts:\n- 2019 champion: Flamengo 90 pts ✓ (real: 90)\n- Top 3: Flamengo, Santos 74, Palmeiras 74 ✓ (real!)\n- 2018 champion Palmeiras ✓\n- 2018 Libertadores final: Boca 2-2 River + River 3-1 Boca ✓ (the famous final!)\n- 2020 Copa do Brasil final: Grêmio 0-1 Palmeiras + Palmeiras 2-0 Grêmio ✓\n- 2019 relegation: Cruzeiro, CSA, Chapecoense, Avaí ✓ — exactly the real relegated teams!\n- Biggest win: Goiás 7-0 Juventude (2003) — real result ✓\n- 2022 Corinthians home: data shows 25 matches 16W — hmm real 2022 Corinthians home: 19 games. 25 matches?! Because team_stats(season=2022) without competition filter spans Serie A (Brasileirao_Matches 2022) + Serie A 2022 from BR-Football? Wait dedupe — 2022 Série A: Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2022) + BR-Football (2014-2023). Dedupe key (comp, season, home, away) → same pairs collapse. But 25 home matches for Corinthians in 2022? That's 19 + 6 extra. Where from? Copa do Brasil 2022 home matches + Libertadores 2022? YES — team_stats has NO competition filter → all competitions. 19 league home + 6 cup/lib home = 25 ✓ correct behavior! (The spec example was \"Corinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão)\" — with competition filter it'd be 19.) Let me verify with competition filter quickly in tests.\n\nEverything looks great. Now:\n1. tools.py — MCP tool wrappers\n2. server.py — FastMCP wiring\n3. __init__.py\n4. Tests (BDD + unit + e2e + sample questions)\n5. requirements.txt, README update\n\ntools.py: functions taking a store (singleton) and returning dicts; list of (name, description, schema) for registration. FastMCP with @mcp.tool() needs direct functions — I'll define them in server.py as thin wrappers around store methods. So tools.py holds the NL router (answer_question) + tool implementations.\n\nActually simpler: server.py defines tools directly calling store methods. The NL router goes into tools.py.\n\nanswer_question(question): deterministic router:\n- normalize q\n- detect year (19xx|20xx)\n- detect two teams → h2h (via known team display names scan)\n- keywords: standings/table/champion/won/relegated → standings(comp, year)\n- players/who is/rating → player query\n- derby → derbies\n- average goals/biggest wins/best home/best away → statistics\n- team record → team_stats\n- fallback: search matches with resolved teams + year\n\nTeam extraction: scan q against display names + raw variants? Keep a list of \"major teams\" (display names, len>3) sorted by length desc; find first two occurrences. Simple and works for demo questions.\n\nLet me write tools.py with answer_question, then server.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b02ea63001Ool08nGg3ZDnSm","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b020235001friJqQWgt5FjhH"}}
