nActually the JSON decode failure might be because the response content is a JSON string that starts fine... \"Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)\" means empty text. If the tool raised an unhandled exception, FastMCP returns an error result (isError=True) with empty content → text empty. What could raise? `answer_question(store, question)` → inside, `store.standings(...)` — `comp not in LEAGUE_COMPETITIONS`? comp = \"Brasileirão Serie A\" ✓. Or... `raise NotFound(\"Which season (year)?...\")` — no, year=2019.\n\nHmm wait — actually, the exception may be `_ok(**answer_question(store, question))` — answer_question returns {\"tool\": ..., \"result\": ...} → _ok(**that) → {\"tool\": ..., \"result\": ...} ✓ fine.\n\nLet me test the router directly in-process.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b0482e10011L7fteKB0SFXRK","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b041079001CRSH4hxMgysAQZ"}}
