orinthians\" — display \"Corinthians\" — hmm `_detect_teams`: q = strip_accents(lower) = \"when did flamengo last play corinthians?\" — display \"Corinthians\" → stripped \"corinthians\" len 11 ≥ 4 → idx = q.find(\"corinthians\") ✓ should find! But wait — Flamengo found first (idx 9), Corinthians (idx 32) — loop `if idx >= last_end` — picked flamengo, last_end = 9+11=20 → corinthians idx 32 ≥ 20 ✓ picked... but then result shows team only, no opponent. Hmm — \"matches\": 920 = Flamengo's total. So teams[1] missing → teams list had 1 element. Why? OH — `strip_accents(\"Flamengo-RJ\")` → \"flamengo-rj\" — but q contains \"flamengo\" not \"flamengo-rj\"! display.find fails for suffixed display names! The display \"Flamengo-RJ\" isn't IN the question text. So only teams whose display matches exactly get found. \"Corinthians\" display = \"Corinthians\" ✓ found... but output shows only team=Flamengo-RJ...\n\n   Wait — if only \"Corinthians\" was found, team would be Corinthians. The result shows 920 matches from 2003 = all matches of team... hmm 920 — Flamengo has ~920 matches. So teams[0] = Flamengo-something. Which display matched? Maybe \"Flamengo\" bare display? No — display is \"Flamengo-RJ\". Hmm — display_names() contains keys → display for \"flamengo|RJ\" = \"Flamengo-RJ\"... find(\"flamengo-rj\") in q → -1. So what matched at idx 9? Maybe another team whose display is \"Flamengo\"? No. OR \"Corinthians\" matched FIRST (only match) → teams[0]=\"Corinthians\", search team=Corinthians → 920?? Corinthians has ~900 matches (2003-2022 + cups) — plausible! And Flamengo NOT found because display \"Flamengo-RJ\" doesn't substring-match \"flamengo\".\n\n   FIX _detect_teams: match on BOTH display name and its \"base\" form (display without state suffix, e.g. \"flamengo\"). For each team, try matching any of {display, display-minus-suffix} but require the base match to be ≥4 chars. Careful with ambiguous clubs: \"Atlético-MG\" → base \"atlético\" — a question mentioning \"Atlético\" (mineiro? PR?) — strip suffix → matches Atlético-MG first (popularity? reading order). Acceptable for demo. Also include strip_accents(display).replace(\"-\",\" \")? Keep simple: match display, or base = display split on \"-\" first part when the display has a state-suffix pattern AND base length ≥ 4.\n\n3. **\"Which players play for Flamengo?\" → search_players 0** — \"for Flamengo\" → team detection failed (same display issue) → fell to name search of whole question → 0. Fixed by (2) → routes to players_at_club(\"Flamengo-RJ\") — but FIFA data has NO Flamengo club (FIFA 19 dataset lacks it!) → total 0. Hmm — spec expects \"Filter FIFA data by Club containing Flamengo\" — the data has no Flamengo players (dataset limitation). The tool should return gracefully: total 0 + note? My players_at_club returns total 0 ✓ graceful. For the sample-question test, I should not assert >0 for Flamengo players; use \"Cruzeiro\"/\"Atlético Mineiro\"/\"Fluminense\"/\"Santos\" instead (they exist). I'll note this in README (data limitation).\n\n   Also improve the router: when players_at_club returns 0, add a \"note\" that the FIFA dataset doesn't cover that club. Let me add that note in players_at_club when total==0: {\"note\": \"No players for this club in the FIFA 19 dataset...\"}.\n\n4. **\"What is Corinthians' home record in 2022?\" → season: 20!!** — `_detect_years` found \"2022\" as years[-1]... but season shows 20 — the group bug again: findall with capturing group returns \"20\"/\"19\" prefixes. Fix regex → (?:19|20)\\d{2}. Also question has \"corinthians'\" apostrophe — fine.\n\n   Also the team-stats branch requires keywords (\"record\" ✓). With year fixed → season 2022 ✓.\n\nFixes to apply:\n- tools.py: _YEAR_RE non-capturing; _detect_teams matching base forms too.\n- store.players_at_club: add note when empty.\n- Also router: \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" → team detected (after fix) → players_at_club ✓.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b0569