{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788233650849,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_a2cc5c07f6674f5db94da0e2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py","newString":"        m = re.search(r\"who\\s+is\\s+(.+?)[\\?\\.!]?$\", question.strip(), re.I)\n        if m:\n            try:\n                return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n                        \"result\": store.get_player(m.group(1).strip())}\n            except NotFound as exc:\n                return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n                        \"result\": {\"found\": False, \"message\": str(exc)}}","oldString":"        m = re.search(r\"who\\s+is\\s+(.+?)[\\?\\.!]?$\", question.strip(), re.I)\n        if m:\n            return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n                    \"result\": store.get_player(m.group(1).strip())}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n@@ -120,10 +120,14 @@\n     return {\"tool\": \"search_players_at_club\",\n             \"result\": store.players_at_club(teams[0])}\n m = re.search(r\"who\\s+is\\s+(.+?)[\\?\\.!]?$\", question.strip(), re.I)\n if m:\n-    return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n-            \"result\": store.get_player(m.group(1).strip())}\n+    try:\n+        return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n+                \"result\": store.get_player(m.group(1).strip())}\n+    except NotFound as exc:\n+        return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n+                \"result\": {\"found\": False, \"message\": str(exc)}}\n if \"brazil\" in q:\n     return {\"tool\": \"search_players\",\n             \"result\": store.search_players(nationality=\"brazil\",\n                                            min_overall=75, limit=10)}\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/tools.py\n@@ -120,10 +120,14 @@\n     return {\"tool\": \"search_players_at_club\",\n             \"result\": store.players_at_club(teams[0])}\n m = re.search(r\"who\\s+is\\s+(.+?)[\\?\\.!]?$\", question.strip(), re.I)\n if m:\n-    return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n-            \"result\": store.get_player(m.group(1).strip())}\n+    try:\n+        return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n+                \"result\": store.get_player(m.group(1).strip())}\n+    except NotFound as exc:\n+        return {\"tool\": \"get_player\",\n+                \"result\": {\"found\": False, \"message\": str(exc)}}\n if \"brazil\" in q:\n     return {\"tool\": \"search_players\",\n             \"result\": store.search_players(nationality=\"brazil\",\n                                            min_overall=75, limit=10)}\n","additions":6,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/tools.py","time":{"start":1788233650845,"end":1788233650847}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good progress:\n- \"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians?\" → 2023-10-08 most recent ✓\n- \"Who is Neymar?\" → Neymar Jr full profile ✓\n- \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" → NotFound raised — the router should return a graceful error dict rather than raising. In server.py's answer_question tool, NotFound is caught → error JSON ✓. But for consistency, the router shouldn't crash. In tests, I'll assert NotFound handling. It's fine — but the router for get_player could catch NotFound and return a structured \"not_found\" result. Let me wrap: in answer_question, wrap get_player call:\n\n```python\nif m:\n    try:\n        return {\"tool\": \"get_player\", \"result\": store.get_player(m.group(1).strip())}\n    except NotFound as exc:\n        return {\"tool\": \"get_player\", \"result\": {\"found\": False, \"message\": str(exc)}}\n```\n\nThat keeps \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" answerable (graceful). Good.\n\nNow write the tests. Plan:\n\n```\ntests/\n├── conftest.py                  # store fixture (session scope)\n├── test_normalize.py            # unit tests: keys, dates, registry\n├── test_loader_and_store.py     # unit: counts, dedupe, indexes, data quality\n├── test_mcp_server.py           # e2e: in-memory MCP session, tools + resources + errors\n├── test_sample_questions.py     # 20+ spec questions end-to-end via router\n├── features/\n│   ├── match_queries.feature\n│   ├── team_queries.feature\n│   ├── player_queries.feature\n│   ├── competition_queries.feature\n│   └── statistics.feature\n└── step_defs/\n    ├── conftest.py\n    ├── test_match_queries.py\n    ├── test_team_queries.py\n    ├── test_player_queries.py\n    ├── test_competition_queries.py\n    └── test_statistics.py\n```\n\npytest-bdd 8.x API: `from pytest_bdd import scenarios, given, when, then, parsers`. `scenarios(\"features/match_queries.feature\")` — the feature file path relative to the test file dir by default. Steps with parsers: `@then(parsers.parse('I should receive a list of {count:d} matches'))` etc.\n\nconftest.py at tests/ root with `store` fixture session-scoped. Since store load is ~0.7s, session scope is important.\n\nBDD scenarios (Gherkin) — cover the two from TASK.md plus more:\n\nmatch_queries.feature:\n- Find matches between two teams (Flamengo/Fluminense) — list non-empty; each has date/scores/competition; h2h summary present\n- Get team statistics (Palmeiras 2023) — wins/losses/draws/goals\n- Find Copa do Brasil finals — stage final, ≥ 2-legged, seasons 2012-2021\n- Find matches by date range\n- Find matches by season (Palmeiras 2023)\n\nteam_queries.feature:\n- Corinthians home record 2022 (venue=home, competition Serie A) — 19 matches? assert >= 15 and goals fields; win rate consistency: wins/matches*100 ≈ win_rate\n- Compare Palmeiras vs Santos head-to-head — totals sum to match count\n- Team history: Palmeiras competitions include Serie A, Copa do Brasil, Libertadores\n- Team not found → NotFound error\n\nplayer_queries.feature:\n- Find all Brazilian players — all nationality Brazil; sorted by overall desc\n- Highest-rated players at a Brazilian club (Cruzeiro) — avg rating; sorted\n- Forwards from São Paulo? FIFA club \"São Paulo\" doesn't exist in dataset... spec example: \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\" — data lacks São Paulo FC! Use position filter on a club that exists (e.g. Grêmio forwards?) — assert position filter works generally: search_players(position=\"ST\", nationality=\"brazil\", min_overall=80)\n- Who is Gabriel Barbosa → NotFound (dataset limitation, graceful)\n- get_player Neymar Jr details\n\ncompetition_queries.feature:\n- Who won 2019 Brasileirão → Flamengo; table 20 rows; 380 matches\n- 2019 relegation zone = [Cruzeiro, CSA, Chapecoense, Avaí]\n- Standings for cup competition → NotFound (Libertadores)\n- 2018 vs 2023 champions comparison\n\nstatistics.feature:\n- Average goals per match in Série A > 2 and < 3\n- Home win rate between 30-60%\n- Biggest wins: margin descending, top entry margin ≥ 5\n- Best away record: win rate ≤ home win rate + tolerance... just assert structure and win_rate ≤ 100\n\ndata_quality.feature (normalization BDD):\n- team name variants resolve to same club (\"Palmeiras-SP\" == \"Palmeiras\")\n- Brazilian date format parsed (novo_campeonato 2003-04-27? \"29/03/2003\")\n- UTF-8 display names (São Paulo, Grêmio, Avaí present)\n- cross-file player+match link (Atlético Mineiro FIFA players ↔ match team key)\n\nUnit tests (non-BDD): normalize functions, loader counts/dedupe, store error paths, performance test (simple lookup < 2s, aggregate < 5s).\n\ntest_sample_questions.py: run ≥ 20 questions from the spec through answer_question + store methods; assert each returns non-empty/valid structure. This directly maps to the \"At least 20 sample questions\" success criterion.\n\ntest_mcp_server.py: use stdio_client in subprocess? That's slow-ish (~1s spawn + load). In-memory: mcp.shared.memory.create_connected_server_and_client_session works with a FastMCP instance? create_connected_server_and_client_session takes a Server (FastMCP has ._mcp_server?). In mcp 1.x FastMCP has `server` property (the low-level Server). Simpler and more realistic: subprocess stdio_client with sys.executable server.py — proves the actual server binary works. It takes ~2s total. Fine.\n\npytest-asyncio needed for async tests? I can run asyncio.run() inside sync test — no plugin needed.\n\nLet me also double-check pytest-bdd 8.1 API compatibility: `scenarios('../features/xxx.feature')` — relative paths resolved relative to the STEP DEFINITION file. In 8.x, feature paths are relative to the calling test file's directory. I'll place step files in tests/step_defs/ and use \"../features/x.feature\".\n\nAlso gherkin parser: pytest-bdd 8 uses gherkin-official ✓ installed.\n\nOne more thing: TASK.md says data files \"must be used\" ✓ all 6 loaded. \"At least 20 sample questions\" ✓ test file. \"Cross-file queries\" ✓ tested (players_at_club with match-team key + statistics). \"Team name variations\" ✓. \"Multiple date formats\" ✓. \"UTF-8\" ✓.\n\nAlso the router: \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" — intent: derby keyword ✓ season 2023 ✓.\n\nFix the get_player graceful handling in router first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b08128f001u4UWK8zV4UTVBH","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b072a3c001pYWbjUDNAXF6BK"}}
