{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788233772960,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_778a687216dd4d7db121c640","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"BDD step definitions for the Match Queries feature.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport pytest\nfrom pytest_bdd import given, parsers, scenarios, when, then\n\nscenarios(\"../features/match_queries.feature\")\n\n\n@given(\"the match data is loaded\")\ndef loaded_store(store):\n    return store\n\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I search for matches between \"{team_a}\" and \"{team_b}\"'))\ndef search_between(store, team_a, team_b):\n    return store.head_to_head(team_a, team_b)\n\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I request the head-to-head record of \"{team_a}\" and \"{team_b}\"'))\ndef request_h2h(store, team_a, team_b):\n    return store.head_to_head(team_a, team_b)\n\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I search for matches of \"{team}\" in season {season:d}'))\ndef search_team_season(store, team, season):\n    return store.search_matches(team=team, season=season, limit=100)\n\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I search for matches between dates \"{start}\" and \"{end}\"'))\ndef search_date_range(store, start, end):\n    return store.search_matches(date_from=start, date_to=end, limit=100)\n\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I search for stage \"{stage}\" in \"{competition}\"'))\ndef search_stage(store, stage, competition):\n    return store.search_matches(stage=stage, competition=competition, limit=100)\n\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I search for stage \"{stage}\" in \"{competition}\" for season {season:d}'))\ndef search_stage_season(store, stage, competition, season):\n    return store.search_matches(stage=stage, competition=competition,\n                                season=season, limit=100)\n\n\n@then(\"I should receive a list of matches\")\ndef assert_match_list(result):\n    assert isinstance(result.get(\"matches\"), list)\n    assert result[\"total\"] > 0\n    assert result[\"matches\"], \"expected at least one match\"\n\n\n@then(\"each match should have date, scores, and competition\")\ndef assert_match_fields(result):\n    for m in result[\"matches\"]:\n        assert m[\"date\"], f\"missing date: {m}\"\n        assert m[\"home_goal\"] is not None and m[\"away_goal\"] is not None\n        assert m[\"competition\"], f\"missing competition: {m}\"\n\n\n@then(\"the response should include a head-to-head summary\")\ndef assert_h2h_summary(result):\n    for field in (\"team_a_wins\", \"team_b_wins\", \"draws\",\n                  \"team_a_goals\", \"team_b_goals\"):\n        assert field in result\n\n\n@then(\"the head-to-head should include wins, draws and goals for both teams\")\ndef assert_h2h_fields(result):\n    assert result[\"team_a_wins\"] + result[\"team_b_wins\"] + result[\"draws\"] \\\n        == result[\"total_matches\"]\n    assert result[\"team_a_goals\"] >= 0 and result[\"team_b_goals\"] >= 0\n\n\n@then(parsers.parse('the rivalry should be recognized as \"{derby_name}\"'))\ndef assert_derby(result, derby_name):\n    assert result[\"derby\"] == derby_name\n\n\n@then(parsers.parse(\"every match should be in season {season:d}\"))\ndef assert_season(result, season):\n    assert result[\"matches\"]\n    for m in result[\"matches\"]:\n        assert m[\"season\"] == season\n\n\n@then(\"every match date should fall within the range\")\ndef assert_date_range(result):\n    assert result[\"matches\"]\n    for m in result[\"matches\"]:\n        assert \"2019-05-01\" <= m[\"date\"] <= \"2019-05-31\"\n\n\n@then(\"every match should be a cup final\")\ndef assert_cup_final(result):\n    assert result[\"matches\"]\n    for m in result[\"matches\"]:\n        assert m[\"stage\"] == \"final\"\n        assert m[\"competition\"] == \"Copa do Brasil\"\n\n\n@then(parsers.parse('the finalists should include \"{team_a}\" and \"{team_b}\"'))\ndef assert_finalists(result, team_a, team_b):\n    names = {m[\"home\"] for m in result[\"matches\"]} | {m[\"away\"] for m in result[\"matches\"]}\n    assert team_a in names and team_b in names\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/tests/step_defs/test_match_queries.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/tests/step_defs/test_match_queries.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"tests/step_defs/test_match_queries.py","time":{"start":1788233772950,"end":1788233772958}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the step definitions. pytest-bdd 8.x syntax:\n\n```python\nfrom pytest_bdd import scenarios, given, when, then, parsers\n\nscenarios(\"../features/match_queries.feature\")\n\n@given(\"the match data is loaded\")\ndef loaded_store(store):\n    return store\n```\n\nNote: in pytest-bdd 8, `given` returns values via return (target fixture name = function name by default; can use @given(\"...\", target_fixture=\"x\")).\n\nWith parsers.parse for parameters:\n```python\n@when(parsers.parse('I search for matches between \"{team_a}\" and \"{team_b}\"'))\ndef search_between(store, team_a, team_b):\n    return store.head_to_head(team_a, team_b)\n```\nThen steps take the previous step's return as a fixture by function name. Chain: the `when` return becomes a fixture named after the function; `then` steps consume it.\n\nAlso need a shared \"ctx\" pattern — simplest: each when returns dict and thens inspect it.\n\nLet me write the step files carefully so each scenario's steps line up. pytest-bdd requires step uniqueness across scenarios per module (steps are module-scoped). Different feature files = different modules ✓.\n\nmatch step defs:\n\n```python\nscenarios(\"../features/match_queries.feature\")\n\n@given(\"the match data is loaded\")\ndef match_store(store):\n    return store\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I search for matches between \"{team_a}\" and \"{team_b}\"'))\ndef search_between(store, team_a, team_b):\n    return store.head_to_head(team_a, team_b)\n```\nHmm — for scenario 1 the example says \"search for matches between\" then \"each match should have date, scores, and competition\" then \"response should include a head-to-head summary\". Using head_to_head result (has matches + h2h summary) satisfies both ✓.\n\nScenario 2 uses the same when text? No — scenario 2: \"I request the head-to-head record of X and Y\" — separate step (can call same method).\n\nThen steps:\n```python\n@then(\"I should receive a list of matches\")\ndef assert_list(result):\n    assert result[\"matches\"]  # for h2h result: result has \"matches\" key ✓\n\n@then(\"each match should have date, scores, and competition\")\ndef assert_fields(result):\n    for m in result[\"matches\"]:\n        assert m[\"date\"] and m[\"competition\"] and m[\"home_goal\"] is not None\n```\n\nCareful: \"I should receive a list of matches\" is used in MANY feature files — each module needs its own definition (module-scoped) — fine, define in each file.\n\ndata_quality feature: steps without a store-based when/given returning things — need distinct names.\n\nNow unit tests:\n\ntest_normalize.py:\n- strip_accents, canonical_key behaviors\n- parse_team_name cases\n- parse_date cases\n- registry: variants merging, ambiguity (botafogo RJ/PB/SP distinct), defaults (bare Botafogo → RJ), country codes (Nacional URU vs PAR vs Nacional-AM), FIFA club link (Atlético Mineiro → atletico|MG)\n\ntest_loader_and_store.py:\n- counts: matches > 15000; players == 18207\n- dedupe: Serie A 2019 == 380, each team 38\n- competition coverage\n- store indexes consistent\n- performance: search_matches < 2s; statistics < 5s\n\ntest_mcp_server.py:\n- spawn subprocess server, stdio_client, initialize, list_tools (14 tools), call get_head_to_head, get_standings, search_players, answer_question, read resource, error case (unknown team → error JSON).\n\ntest_sample_questions.py: 20+ questions via answer_question/store with assertions each is \"answered\" (non-empty, no exception, structured). Include the exact spec questions list:\n\n1. Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches → h2h\n2. What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023? → search\n3. Find all Copa do Brasil finals → stage search\n4. What is Corinthians' home record in 2022? → team_stats\n5. Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023? → standings row max gf\n6. Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head → h2h\n7. Find all Brazilian players in the dataset → search_players\n8. Who are the highest-rated players at Cruzeiro? → players_at_club\n9. Who won the 2019 Brasileirão? → standings\n10. Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores bracket → finals (stage final = final pair)\n11. Which teams were relegated in 2020? → standings relegation\n12. What's the average goals per match in the Brasileirão? → statistics\n13. Which team has the best away record? → statistics\n14. Show me the biggest wins in the dataset → statistics\n15. When did Flamengo last play Corinthians? → search desc\n16. What was the score? (needs context — skip? It's contextual. Replace with: \"What was the score of the last Flamengo vs Corinthians match?\" → h2h tail)\n17. Who is Gabriel Barbosa? → graceful not-found ✓ (spec explicitly lists it!)\n18. Which players play for Fluminense? → players_at_club\n19. Show me all derbies in 2023 → derbies\n20. What competitions has Palmeiras played in? → team_history\n21. Which team has the best home record? → statistics\n22. Who are the top Brazilian players? → search_players sorted\n23. Compare the 2018 and 2019 seasons → compare_seasons\n24. Show the 2019 Brasileirão final standings → standings\n\nThat's 24 ✓. Test asserts each returns data (non-empty or explicitly-structured).\n\nAlso a pytest marker for slow? Not needed.\n\nOrder: write unit tests first, then steps, then run.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b09ef8f001SrqB8qb663hliW","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b09026