{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788233876743,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_73dbd992927840889ab3707c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"BDD step definitions for the Data Quality feature.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport pytest\nfrom pytest_bdd import given, parsers, scenarios, when, then\n\nfrom brazilian_soccer.normalize import parse_date\n\nscenarios(\"../features/data_quality.feature\")\n\n\n@given(\"the team registry is finalized\")\ndef registry_ready(store):\n    return store.registry\n\n\n@given(parsers.parse('a Brazilian formatted date \"{raw}\"'), target_fixture=\"date_raw\")\ndef given_brazilian_date(raw):\n    return raw\n\n\n@given(parsers.parse('an ISO datetime \"{raw}\"'), target_fixture=\"date_raw\")\ndef given_iso_datetime(raw):\n    return raw\n\n\n@given(\"the store is loaded\")\ndef loaded_store(store):\n    return store\n\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I resolve \"{name_a}\" and \"{name_b}\"'))\ndef resolve_two(store, name_a, name_b):\n    return {\"a\": store.resolve_team(name_a), \"b\": store.resolve_team(name_b)}\n\n\n@when(\"I check the display names\")\ndef check_displays(store):\n    return {\"displays\": set(store.registry.display_names().values())}\n\n\n@when(parsers.parse('I query the FIFA club \"{club}\"'))\ndef query_fifa_club(store, club):\n    key = store.resolve_team(club)\n    return {\n        \"key\": key,\n        \"match_count\": len(store.matches_by_team.get(key, [])),\n        \"player_count\": len(store.players_by_club.get(key, [])),\n    }\n\n\n@when(\"I parse the date\")\ndef parse_the_date(date_raw):\n    return {\"date\": parse_date(date_raw)}\n\n\n@then(\"both names should resolve to the same club\")\ndef assert_same_club(resolved):\n    assert resolved[\"a\"] == resolved[\"b\"]\n\n\n@then(\"the names should resolve to different clubs\")\ndef assert_different_clubs(resolved):\n    assert resolved[\"a\"] != resolved[\"b\"]\n\n\n@then(parsers.parse(\"the parsed date should be {expected}\"))\ndef assert_parsed_date(parsed, expected):\n    assert str(parsed[\"date\"]) == expected\n\n\n@then(parsers.parse('the names \"{n1}\", \"{n2}\" and \"{n3}\" should be present'))\ndef assert_utf8_names(checked, n1, n2, n3):\n    for name in (n1, n2, n3):\n        assert name in checked[\"displays\"], f\"{name} not in display names\"\n\n\n@then(\"the players should link to the same club that appears in match data\")\ndef assert_cross_file_link(queried):\n    assert queried[\"player_count\"] > 0, \"expected FIFA players for the club\"\n    assert queried[\"match_count\"] > 0, \"expected matches for the same club key\"\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/tests/step_defs/test_data_quality.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/tests/step_defs/test_data_quality.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"tests/step_defs/test_data_quality.py","time":{"start":1788233876734,"end":1788233876739}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Hmm — the `_parse` helper with `request.getfixturevalue` is fragile: \"brazilian_date\" won't be in `request.fixturenames` because the when step doesn't depend on the given fixture automatically. In pytest-bdd, given steps create fixtures; the when step function must REQUEST them as parameters. Simpler approach: define the when step with both fixtures as params:\n\n```python\n@when(\"I parse the date\")\ndef parse_the_date(brazilian_date):\n    ...\n```\nBut the ISO scenario's given is \"an ISO datetime ...\" (different fixture). The when step \"I parse the date\" is shared by both scenarios but the given differs. pytest-bdd: if the when function requests fixture `brazilian_date`, the ISO scenario fails (fixture not defined for that scenario).\n\nCleaner: make the given steps both target the SAME fixture name with different parsers:\n```python\n@given(parsers.parse('a Brazilian formatted date \"{raw}\"'), target_fixture=\"date_raw\")\ndef _g1(raw): return raw\n\n@given(parsers.parse('an ISO datetime \"{raw}\"'), target_fixture=\"date_raw\")\ndef _g2(raw): return raw\n\n@when(\"I parse the date\")\ndef parse_the_date(date_raw):\n    return {\"date\": parse_date(date_raw)}\n```\ntarget_fixture makes the given's return available under \"date_raw\" regardless of which given ran. Let me rewrite the data_quality step file accordingly. Also remove unused imports (pytest, given unused? given used ✓; pytest unused).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b0b84f7001g9OFIpQWjEA03L","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b0b330a001cUX9ffUlIDlB60"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788233876743,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"id":"prt_05b0b610c001t4fTttb1JtXJGl","messageID":"msg_05b0b330a001cUX9ffUlIDlB60","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","type":"text","text":"The date-parsing step needs `target_fixture` to unify the two Given variants. Rewriting that file cleanly:","time":{"start":1788233867532,"end":1788233876741}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1788233876910,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"id":"prt_05b0b85ac001mMkebl7HscJ1ut","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"72d33820e31db942b850c742306aa46ae8af0c39","messageID":"msg_05b0b330a001cUX9ffUlIDlB60","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":218731,"input":747,"output":644,"reasoning":316,"cache":{"write":0,"read":217024}},"cost":0.003551385}}
