{"type":"text","timestamp":1788233988201,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"id":"prt_05b0cf95f0016e67kbZEgyxQXf","messageID":"msg_05b0ca286001kf1tc1CQmBM1KM","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","type":"text","text":"The MCP test's event-loop handling is broken (streams bind to the loop that created them). Rewriting with a single module-scoped loop:","time":{"start":1788233972063,"end":1788233988199}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788233988206,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_eaa2b8f11c85423ebdac0ff5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"End-to-end test: the real MCP server over stdio, driven by an MCP client.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom mcp import ClientSession, StdioServerParameters\nfrom mcp.client.stdio import stdio_client\n\nSERVER = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))),\n                      \"server.py\")\nREPO = os.path.dirname(SERVER)\n\nEXPECTED_TOOLS = {\n    \"search_matches\", \"get_head_to_head\", \"get_team_stats\", \"get_team_history\",\n    \"list_teams\", \"get_competitions\", \"get_standings\", \"compare_seasons\",\n    \"search_players\", \"get_player\", \"search_players_at_club\",\n    \"get_statistics\", \"get_derbies\", \"answer_question\",\n}\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef mcp():\n    \"\"\"One server process + MCP session for the whole module.\"\"\"\n    loop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\n    params = StdioServerParameters(command=sys.executable, args=[SERVER], cwd=REPO)\n    cm = stdio_client(params)\n\n    async def _start():\n        read, write = await cm.__aenter__()\n        client_cm = ClientSession(read, write)\n        session = await client_cm.__aenter__()\n        await session.initialize()\n        return client_cm, session\n\n    client_cm, session = loop.run_until_complete(_start())\n    holder = {\"loop\": loop, \"session\": session, \"client_cm\": client_cm, \"cm\": cm}\n    yield holder\n\n    async def _stop():\n        await client_cm.__aexit__(None, None, None)\n        await cm.__aexit__(None, None, None)\n\n    loop.run_until_complete(_stop())\n    loop.close()\n\n\ndef _call(holder, tool: str, args: dict) -> dict:\n    res = holder[\"loop\"].run_until_complete(\n        holder[\"session\"].call_tool(tool, args))\n    return json.loads(res.content[0].text)\n\n\ndef test_server_lists_all_tools(mcp):\n    res = mcp[\"loop\"].run_until_complete(mcp[\"session\"].list_tools())\n    names = {t.name for t in res.tools}\n    assert EXPECTED_TOOLS <= names\n\n\ndef test_search_matches_tool(mcp):\n    data = _call(mcp, \"search_matches\",\n                 {\"team\": \"Flamengo\", \"season\": 2023, \"limit\": 5})\n    assert data[\"total\"] > 0\n    assert data[\"matches\"][0][\"season\"] == 2023\n\n\ndef test_head_to_head_tool(mcp):\n    data = _call(mcp, \"get_head_to_head\",\n                 {\"team_a\": \"Flamengo\", \"team_b\": \"Fluminense\"})\n    assert data[\"derby\"] == \"Fla-Flu\"\n    assert data[\"total_matches\"] > 30\n\n\ndef test_standings_tool(mcp):\n    data = _call(mcp, \"get_standings\",\n                 {\"competition\": \"Brasileirão Serie A\", \"season\": 2019, \"top\": 3})\n    assert data[\"champion\"] == \"Flamengo-RJ\"\n\n\ndef test_player_tool(mcp):\n    data = _call(mcp, \"get_player\", {\"name\": \"Neymar Jr\"})\n    assert data[\"name\"] == \"Neymar Jr\"\n    assert data[\"overall\"] == 92\n\n\ndef test_answer_question_tool(mcp):\n    data = _call(mcp, \"answer_question\",\n                 {\"question\": \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?\"})\n    assert data[\"result\"][\"champion\"] == \"Flamengo-RJ\"\n\n\ndef test_error_is_structured_json(mcp):\n    data = _call(mcp, \"get_team_stats\", {\"team\": \"Narnia United\"})\n    assert \"error\" in data\n\n\ndef test_status_resource(mcp):\n    from mcp.types import AnyUrl\n\n    async def _run():\n        return await mcp[\"session\"].read_resource(AnyUrl(\"soccer://status\"))\n\n    res = mcp[\"loop\"].run_until_complete(_run())\n    data = json.loads(res.contents[0].text)\n    assert data[\"matches\"] > 15000\n    assert data[\"players\"] == 18207\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/tests/test_mcp_server.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/tests/test_mcp_server.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"tests/test_mcp_server.py","time":{"start":1788233988197,"end":1788233988205}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Hmm, my session fixture with `asyncio.new_event_loop()` per test is messy — creating a new event loop for each call while the connection lives on a DIFFERENT loop won't work (anyio streams are loop-bound). Better approach: one event loop for the module, run everything on it:\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef loop():\n    loop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\n    yield loop\n    loop.close()\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef session(loop):\n    async def _run():\n        async with stdio_client(params) as (read, write):\n            async with ClientSession(read, write) as s:\n                await s.initialize()\n                yield s  # hmm, yields inside async with — need to keep the context alive\n```\n\nAsync context managers + yield inside: the async generator pattern works with `loop.run_until_complete(agen.__anext__())` calls on the SAME loop ✓. My original code created a new event loop in the fixture but then each test created ANOTHER new loop via `new_event_loop()` — those tests' calls would fail (streams bound to fixture loop). Also `test_server_lists_all_tools` creates a throwaway loop — wrong.\n\nCleaner: use pytest-asyncio? Not installed. Simplest robust: single module-scoped event loop fixture; session fixture starts the server ON that loop via `run_until_complete(agen.__anext__())`; tests take (session, loop) and use loop.run_until_complete(...). But pytest-bdd/pytest fixtures — tests must request loop too. Let me restructure: give each test a helper `run(session, coro)` where the loop is stored on the session object (e.g., attach as attribute). \n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef mcp():\n    loop = asyncio.new_event_loop()\n    holder = {}\n\n    async def _start():\n        params = StdioServerParameters(command=sys.executable, args=[SERVER], cwd=...)\n        cm = stdio_client(params)\n        read, write = await cm.__aenter__()\n        client_cm = ClientSession(read, write)\n        s = await client_cm.__aenter__()\n        await s.initialize()\n        return cm, client_cm, s\n\n    cm, client_cm, s = loop.run_until_complete(_start())\n    holder[\"cms\"] = (cm, client_cm)\n    holder[\"session\"] = s\n    holder[\"loop\"] = loop\n    yield holder\n    async def _stop():\n        await client_cm.__aexit__(None, None, None)\n        await cm.__aexit__(None, None, None)\n    loop.run_until_complete(_stop())\n    loop.close()\n```\n\nTests:\n```python\ndef test_x(mcp):\n    loop, s = mcp[\"loop\"], mcp[\"session\"]\n    res = loop.run_until_complete(s.call_tool(...))\n```\n\nThis is explicit and reliable. Note: ClientSession enters with `async with` — use __aenter__ directly ✓.\n\nRewrite test_mcp_server.py accordingly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b0d385f001Q2oT3fqOSaD7gZ","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b0ca286001kf1tc1CQmBM1KM"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1788233988386,"sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","part":{"id":"prt_05b0d39210010cbEGpVQOUFUKy","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"a18e0f49c9c245f7477a9a313b6421a8818ca673","messageID":"msg_05b0ca286001kf1tc1CQmBM1KM","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":223952,"input":1097,"output":980,"reasoning":627,"cache":{"write":0,"read":221248}},"cost":0.003802745}}
