 becomes a fixture whose name is the function name ONLY if... Actually in pytest-bdd (all versions), the returned value from a `given` becomes a fixture named after the function (or target_fixture). For `when`/`then` steps, the return value is available to LATER steps via the step function's name as a fixture — yes, that's documented behavior (\"Steps can request the results of previous steps by using their function names as fixtures\"). \n\nThe error says fixture 'result' not found in test_get_team_statistics. The scenario:\n\n```\nScenario: Get team statistics\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2023\"\n    Then I should receive wins, losses, draws, and goals\n```\n\nthen step `assert_record_fields(result)` — requests fixture `result` — the when function is named `team_season_stats`, NOT `result`! I named functions inconsistently: the when step in match_queries was named `search_between` while the then expected `result`. In pytest-bdd, the fixture name is the STEP FUNCTION's name. So I need consistent naming: when-step functions must be named `result` (or thens must reference the actual name). Multiple when functions can't share one name in a module (Python redefinition!). Solution: use `target_fixture=\"result\"` on every when decorator — pytest-bdd supports `@when(..., target_fixture=\"result\")`. Then the when's return is exposed as fixture `result`.\n\nLet me add `target_fixture=\"result\"` to all when step decorators in all 5 step files. For data_quality file: when steps produce fixtures `resolved`, `checked`, `queried`, `parsed` — those use custom names consistently; add target_fixture for each accordingly (or rename). I'll use target_fixture uniformly: \"result\" for the 4 query files, and specific names for data_quality (resolved/checked/queried/parsed — already consistent between when and then; but the when functions' own names differ from those fixture names → also need target_fixture).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b10d32e001Fgr6KPHVeV1p5D","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b108385001GZpb8jPEnfl4G4"}}
