art":1788234286847,"end":1788234286850}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Multiple remaining issues:\n\n1. **data_quality file: 'resolved'/'parsed'/'checked'/'queried' not found** — same target_fixture issue: my when functions are named `resolve_two` etc. but thens request `resolved`. Need target_fixture on those when decorators: `target_fixture=\"resolved\"`, `\"checked\"`, `\"queried\"`, `\"parsed\"`.\n\n2. **team_queries: StepDefinitionNotFoundError for \"the head-to-head should include wins, draws and goals for both teams\"** — the when decorator for team h2h spans two lines with the string on the second line; my earlier regex DID handle it (line 22 shows it patched). The missing step: team_queries.feature scenario \"Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\" has then-step \"the head-to-head should include wins, draws and goals for both teams\" — but I defined that then-step in test_MATCH_queries.py, not team_queries! Steps are module-scoped — team_queries.py needs its own copy. I have `assert_h2h_fields` only in match file. Add to team file.\n\n3. **KeyError 'total' in statistics biggest_wins then-step** — my step: `result[\"biggest_wins\"]` — statistics() response HAS \"biggest_wins\" key ✓... KeyError 'total' — the failing step is \"I should receive a descending list of victories\"? No: `assert_wins_desc(result)` accesses `result[\"biggest_wins\"]` → wins items have \"match\" key: `w[\"match\"][\"home_goal\"]` — the stats biggest_wins items are {\"date\",\"winner\",\"score\",\"loser\",\"competition\"} — no \"match\" key! I wrote the then-step expecting internal objects. Fix the step to use score/winner fields, or better: assert using \"score\" strings: margin = parse ints. Rewrite assert_wins_desc: margins from score strings. And assert_top_margin similarly.\n\n   KeyError 'total' — where? test_biggest_victories: then \"I should receive a descending list of victories\" — my step name matches ✓... KeyError 'total' hmm — maybe from test_match_queries/test_player_queries? Two KeyError 'total' lines. `players_at_club` response has no \"total\" key — the player file's then \"I should receive a list of players\" asserts `result[\"total\"] > 0` — players_at_club response has \"total_players\" not \"total\"! Fix: make players_at_club response include \"total\" too, or make the step tolerant. Better: align response shape — add \"total\" to players_at_club? It already has total_players. I'll update the player when-step for club to re-shape: return {\"players\": ..., \"total\": ...}. Simplest: in the step file, `players_at_club` when-step wraps: r = store.players_at_club(club); return {\"players\": r[\"players\"], \"total\": r[\"total_players\"]}. But then \"the players should have an average rating\" needs average_overall — include it.\n\n   test_find_matches_between_two_teams KeyError 'total': match file scenario 1 uses head_to_head response — which has \"total_matches\" not \"total\"! The then \"I should receive a list of matches\" asserts result[\"total\"] > 0. Fix: make the when-step for scenario 1 return a normalized dict: {\"matches\": h2h[\"matches\"], \"total\": len, plus h2h fields}. Cleanest: have store.head_to_head include \"total\" as alias. I'll add \"total\": len(selected) to the h2h response — harmless, helps consistency.\n\n4. **test_competition_catalog failure** — need detail. Probably then-step \"the catalog should include ...\" — result fixture = competitions() response which has \"competitions\" key ✓... assert uses result[\"competitions\"] ✓. Hmm, let me look after fixes.\n\nLet me apply fixes:\n- data_quality: add target_fixture to when decorators.\n- team_queries: add the h2h-fields then-step.\n- statistics: fix biggest-wins assertions to use the serialized fields.\n- store.head_to_head: add \"total\" key.\n- player queries: reshape players_at_club in the when step (or add \"total\" alias in store). I'll add \"total\" alias in store.players_at_club response too — consistent API.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b11c6c00014fFQ9uugt6V3xx","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b11410a001mWoc1V9CSaxwZ3"}}
