occer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-0bivsr25/retort-e0c09c17c08e/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -201,9 +201,17 @@\n     return rows\n \n \n def dedupe_matches(matches: list[Match]) -> list[Match]:\n-    \"\"\"Keep one row per real match, preferring richer sources.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Keep one row per real match, preferring richer sources.\n+\n+    A row with an actual score always wins over a resultless row of a\n+    higher-priority source (the Brasileirão CSV contains postponed games\n+    with empty scores that other datasets resolve).\n+    \"\"\"\n+    def rank(m: Match) -> tuple[int, int]:\n+        return (0 if m.has_result() else 1, SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(m.source, 9))\n+\n     best: dict[tuple, Match] = {}\n     for m in matches:\n         if m.competition.startswith(\"Brasileirão Serie\"):\n             key = (\"league\", m.competition, m.season, m.home_key, m.away_key)\n@@ -211,10 +219,9 @@\n             key = (\"cup\", m.season, m.date, m.home_key, m.away_key)\n         else:\n             key = (\"libertadores\", id(m))      # single source: no dedupe\n         cur = best.get(key)\n-        if cur is None or SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(m.source, 9) < \\\n-                SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(cur.source, 9):\n+        if cur is None or rank(m) < rank(cur):\n             best[key] = m\n     return list(best.values())\n \n \n","additions":10,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/loader.py","time":{"start":1788234425776,"end":1788234425777}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Four failures:\n\n1. **test_04: Corinthians home record 2022 = 15, expected 19** — with competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\" 2022 → 15 home matches?! 2022 Série A should be 19 home. Why 15? Because team_stats filters by competition — \"Brasileirão Serie A\" 2022 matches: Brasileirao_Matches (380) + BR-Football 2022 Serie A. Dedupe key (comp, season, home, away)... wait earlier standings test for 2022 said 380 ✓ and Corinthians has 38 league matches. Home league = 19. But team_stats with venue=home gives 15?? Because team_stats competition filter uses resolve_competition(\"Brasileirão Serie A\") = BRASILEIRAO_A ✓. Hmm — but wait: Corinthians 2022: some home matches missing results? 4 resultless rows in 2022 from Brasileirao_Matches (postponed games: Sao Paulo-Coritiba, Cuiaba-Flamengo, Corinthians-Athletico-PR!, Internacional-Goias...) — those 2022 rows with no goals! team_record skips matches without result. Corinthians home 2022: 19 fixtures, 4? resultless → 15 with results. AH — but wait: were those 4 resultless Brasileirao_Matches rows the ONLY record of those fixtures? If BR-Football 2022 has them WITH results, dedupe would keep Brasileirao_Matches (priority 1) — dropping the resultful BR-Football row!! PRIORITY BUG: I should prefer the row WITH a result when priorities conflict. Fix dedupe: prefer (has_result) first, then source priority. Actually — better ranking: (not has_result, source_priority). This also fixes the 2016 Chapecoense row (if another source has the actual result... the 2016 match was suspended — only played later 2017-03-04? it may exist in BR-Football 2016 with result). Let me apply: dedupe prefers matches with results.\n\n   Hmm wait — but earlier performance test: standings 2022 = 380 with all results? If some Brasileirao_Matches rows lack results and BR-Football has them, standings table would count fewer matches. Standings for 2022: total_matches_used was 380 but has_result rows maybe fewer. Fixing dedupe solves this.\n\n2. **test_11: relegation 2020** — got Botafogo-RJ instead of Athletico-PR in the bottom 4. Athletico-PR 2020: real relegation was Vasco, Goiás, Coritiba, Athletico-PR (17th Athletico-PR with 41 pts... wait actually 2020 relegation: Vasco, Goiás, Coritiba, Athletic