ter dedupe... whatever).\n\nRoot fix: my \"final = max round within season\" heuristic breaks when the file lacks later rounds. Better heuristic for the cup: the final = the LAST round chronologically per season (by max date among that season's matches)? For 2021: the last-played round = round 4 (file truncates in July?) — also wrong.\n\nAlternative: use a canonical ROUND COUNT per edition: Copa do Brasil editions 2012-2021 all had: round 1-2 preliminary (varies), ..., final. The number of rounds VARIES by year (2012: 8 rounds? 2013+: 7 rounds: 1,2,3,4,5(semis?),6?; hmm). Actually Copa do Brasil format 2013-2015: 7 rounds (R1 64 teams? no...). Formats:\n- 2012: 64 teams, 5 national rounds? no — 2012: rounds 1-8?? Cup 2012: First round 64 teams (32 ties), second 32, third 16, round of 16, QF, SF, Final = 7 rounds.\n- Hmm but data shows rounds up to 8 (2012-2013?) — 2013 had preliminary rounds adding up.\n\nI can't rely on fixed counts. Robust approach: define stage by round from the END using per-season round ranking ONLY when the season's round set forms a complete knockout pyramid (40→20→32?? no).\n\nWait actually — look at 2021 rounds: 1:40, 2:20, 3:32, 4:16 — this is NOT a simple halving because of byes/seeding (32 teams enter at round 3). The real 2021 edition had 6 rounds total (R1, R2, R3, R4, SF=R5? no...). Copa do Brasil 2021 rounds: First(40), Second(20+12 seeded → 32 ties at Third?) hmm: 2021: Round 1: 80 teams → 40 ties; Round 2: 40 winners → 20 ties; then 12 seeded teams join 20 winners → 32 teams → Round 3: 16 ties?? But data shows round 3: 32 matches, round 4: 16. So data's round numbering differs from real rounds. File round 4 (16 matches) = real Round 3? I'm lost in format details.\n\nPRAGMATIC approach: define the final per season as the round whose ties' winners played the latest... no data. Alternative: use KNOWN final counts: the final is the last round of each edition; editions 2012-2021. For seasons 2012-2019 the max-round heuristic produced exactly 2 finals each ✓ (from the Counter: 2012-2020 all 2!). Only 2021 is broken (16 round-4 matches). Special-case: 2021's real final (Atlético-MG × Athletico-PR, Dec 2021) lives in BR-Football only. So: for seasons where max-round yields >2 matches, the file is truncated → derive finals from BR-Football rows instead: the LAST round chronologically per (season)... the 2021 final: 2 legs, dates Dec 12 & 19? within BR-Football cup rows, the latest-date round group. Heuristic: for a cup season, if the count of max-round matches != 2, find BR-Football-only rows in the season, group by date, take the last two?? Fragile.\n\nBetter: GIVE UP the generic \"stage\" derivation for seasons where data is incomplete, and label by round-rank only when a clean pyramid exists: compute stage for matches of a season ONLY IF the season's round sequence is complete. Simplest robust: label \"final\" = matches in the maximum round of the season **only if that round has exactly 2 matches in the deduped data**; if not, look at BR-Football cup rows for that season: take the two latest-dated matches IF they share the same two teams in home/away swapped orientation (a two-legged final!) → label those as final. For 2021: BR-Football has Atlético-MG×Athletico-PR twice (Dec 2021) ✓ → final detected.\n\nHmm — but is the earlier \"round 4 = 16 matches\" mislabeling acceptable as \"round 4\" stage? With the != 2 check, those get stage \"round 4\" (not final) ✓ no false finals.\n\nAlso 2020: file shows 2 finals ✓ (Feb/Mar 2021 legs with season 2020 ✓ after fix).\n\nImplement derive_cup_stages v2:\n1. Group cup matches by season.\n2. max_round per season (from matches with rounds).\n3. For each season: candidates = matches with round == max_round. If len(candidates) == 2 → stage final for them; others: semifinals = max_round-1 (2 matches? not guaranteed) — keep stage labels simple: if max-round count == 2 → those are final; round max-1 → semifinal; max-2 → quarterfinal; else \"round N\". If max-round count != 2 → label ALL rounds plainly (\"round N\") and then attempt the two-legged BR-Football tail: find pairs of matches with identical team sets and the two latest distinct dates in the season → label \"final\".\n4. BR-Football-only rows keep stage None unless matched by the tail rule.\n\nLet me also make Libertadores stage untouched ✓ (given).\n\nEdge: 2012 season: rounds 1-8, max 8: 2 matches ✓ final. Semis round 7: 4 matches → \"semifinals\" ✓. OK.\n\nImplement.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b192673001hj37SjPIkXSI7z","sessionID":"ses_fa52b88b3ffeUF09L5H3uZ1cg4","messageID":"msg_05b17f40a001OFLsQIvZ3BOXAq"}}
